ember carries the same embedded **HCFG** config blob: `'HCFG' | u8 ver | u8 xor_key | u16 len (LE) |\n  u32 crc32 | xor'd JSON` (JSON at offset 12; crc32 is over the decoded plaintext). Only its storage location changes\n  (`.hcfg` section on D2/D10/D14, .NET FieldRVA array, Go/Rust rodata, base64'd in a Java/Kotlin constant pool, base64 Swift/Nim/D/\n  Crystal String literal in `.rodata` on D8/D9/D11/D13, RAW in FPC `.data` on D12). Scan raw bytes for `HCFG` AND for its base64\n  form `SENGR...` (raw `HCFG` can also be a false hit inside code: check crc).\n  The JSON also carries never-asked keys (ipv4, windows_path, linux_path, service, host_model on D7): parse the whole dict so a new `config_<key>` id is free.\n- The analysis is easy (headers, symbols, one config blob). The hard part is the GM's exact label for a few `exact_text` fields (format,\n  machine, disassembly, symbol). The question set grows +10/day from D8 (80 → 90 → ... → 140 on D14); old groups reuse the same\n  bytes, but D8 BACKFILLED old groups to 10 ids each (new: has_symtab, has_cpp_typeinfo/vtable, xor_key_hex, hcfg_version, compression_methods).\n- **The prompt's language theme has NOT been asked since D4** (Rust panics, Kotlin \"state machine\", Swift \"protocols\", Nim\n  \"runtime fingerprints\", D \"templates\", Pascal \"record layouts\", Crystal \"DNS labels\", ObjC \"classes/selectors/persistence\n  descriptor\"). The new group gets sha256, format, architecture, machine, config_campaign/domain/mutex/url/crc32_hex + ONE\n  rotating extra id from a small pool: hcfg_version (D6-D7), `hcfg_offset` (D9, D11-D13), `has_hcfg_section` (D10, D14),\n  elf_class/machine as INTEGERS (D8-D9). D11-D14 introduced NO never-seen field: grep the new group's ids against the solver's\n  field table before anything else; if all are known, run the carried-over solver and submit.\n- Time Trial ≈ 6-16 s early; Mastery = `setN.` prefixed copies, 2 sets through D7, 5 sets / 400-450 ids on D8-D9, 3 sets / 300-420\n  ids on D10-D14 (TT 30 s; D13 TT 80 s / Mastery 200 s; D14 both 30 s); artifacts are named `delivery N: evidence.zip`.\n- **D10 RELAXED the label fields**: 36 ids are now `kind: pattern` whose syntax ACCEPTS equivalents (format: \"ELF or PE; case,\n  ELF32/ELF64/PE32/PE32+ accepted\"; machine/architecture: \"standard tool or symbolic label, or decimal/hex code\"; e_type and\n  endianness: symbolic constant / readelf label / numeric code; .NET format: any container_runtime token with CLI/CLR/.NET). D8-D9's\n  integer machine became pattern. Keep emitting the GM-confirmed spellings; the old REJECTED lists may be stale for pattern ids.\n  (D14: `dNN_analysis_format` is still `exact_text` -> `elf`.)\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **HCFG location / encoding** -- same blob, different storage per container (`.hcfg` section, .NET FieldRVA, Go/Rust rodata,\n  base64 inside a Java/Kotlin constant pool, base64 Swift/Nim/D/Crystal string literal in ELF `.rodata`, raw FPC `.data`): scan raw\n  bytes for `HCFG` and for `SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]*=*` (base64 of `HCFG`, std or urlsafe), decode, accept only if crc32(plain)\n  matches AND the JSON parses -- keep scanning past a failing hit (D9 Nim had two raw `HCFG` decoys); never a fixed offset.\n  Storage did NOT change across a day's variants on any day so far (D14 `.hcfg` at file 0xfa0 in single/TT/all 3 sets).\n- **Location-as-answer (`hcfg_offset`, D9/D11-D13)** -- base-10 FILE offset of the first byte of the stored blob as it sits in\n  the member: base64 form -> the `S` of `SENGR...` (D9 Nim 30696, D11 D 368272, D13 Crystal 560188 -- the text, not the String\n  header 12 B before it); RAW form -> the `H` of `HCFG` (D12 FPC 82928). Constant across a day's variants although shas differ --\n  still compute it: record `m.start()` of whichever scan hit (raw OR base64) validated, on BOTH paths (D12's raw path returned `none`).\n- **Any other storage encoding -> `lib.binary.hcfg_scan(data, deadline=None)`** (pure stdlib, ~15 ms / 2 MB, ~0.6 s / 67 MB).\n  Returns every `HcfgHit` (offset, encoding, version, key, length, crc, crc_ok, config, plain, speculative, detail) best first;\n  take `lib.binary.hcfg_find(data)` (first crc-valid + JSON-parsing hit). Covers raw, base64 (std/url/wrapped), hex (plain, `48 43`,\n  `48:43`, `\\x48`, `0x48, `), base32, base85, ascii85, UTF-16LE/BE of those, reversed raw/base64, single-byte xor'd base64/raw,\n  zlib, gzip, raw deflate. Decoys come back `valid=False`. Offset convention per encoding (`hcfg_offset`):\n\n  | encoding | offset = | status |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | raw | the `H` of the magic | GM-confirmed (D12) |\n  | base64 | first base64 char (`S` of `SENGR`) | GM-confirmed (D9/D11/D13) |\n  | base64url, base32, base85, hex, hex-sep | first char of the stored text (`\\` of `\\x48`, `0` of `0x48`) | speculative |\n  | ascii85 | the `<` of `<~` if present, else first char | speculative |\n  | utf16le-* / utf16be-* | first byte of the first code unit (BE: its `00`); LE/BE tie -> the 2-aligned reading, else LE | speculative |\n  | reversed-raw / reversed-base64 | lowest file offset of the reversed region | speculative |\n  | xor-base64 / xor-raw | first stored byte (`detail` = `xor=0x..`) | speculative |\n  | zlib / gzip / deflate | first byte of the compressed stream | speculative |\n\n  Wired into the binary solver as a fallback (kill switch `HCTF_HCFG_SCAN_EXT=0`); not needed on D14. A speculative offset is a\n  first guess: if rejected, try the offset of the container header in front of the stored form next. Fixtures: `tests/data/hcfg_fixtures/`.\n- **xor key / config values** -- re-roll per variant (`BRNN-00V`, `node-00V.dayNN...`, crc); derive from the header byte, never\n  from the sample. D13 key = 0x91+N; D14 single BR14-000 key 0xa1, TT BR14-002, Mastery BR14-002/007/004.\n- **Container per member** -- ELF vs PE32+ `.exe` re-rolls per member: Mastery set2 had d02 C++ as `.exe` (D3-D5, D7, D10) and d04\n  Go as `.exe` (D4, D5, D7, D10); D10 set2 had the NEW d10 Zig member as a PE too (format `pe`). Labels come from the header of\n  THIS member (Go PE: format `pe`, architecture `x86-64` from Machine).\n- **Variant index per group** -- `dNN--variant-XXX` re-rolls per group and mode; sizes and config values change, names/layout\n  don't. TT often == Mastery set1 bytes (D7, D9, D14: TT and set1 both BR14-002); a carry-over d01 can differ (D9 Mastery d01\n  `mov eax, 8104`). Pair members by sha256, never by index.\n- **Mastery packaging** -- `setN.` prefixed ids, each set its own `delivery N: evidence.zip` (same filename): pair by sha256.\n  Set count re-rolls: 2 (D2-D7), 5 (D8-D9), 3 (D10-D14): loop over every `setN.`. From D9 the first question of each set ends\n  `Evidence case: dNN-m-<16hex>. [assigned-artifact-sha256:<zip sha256>]` (TT: `dNN-tt-...`): an explicit set -> delivery map;\n  it is question TEXT, never part of an answer.\n- **answer_format.kind for the same field name** -- D8: `d01_analysis_elf_class`/`machine` exact_text (`ELF64`/`x86-64`) and\n  `d08_analysis_elf_class`/`machine` integer (`64`/`62`) in ONE contract. Rule: dispatch on `kind`, not on the field name.\n- **Feature-presence fields** -- `has_<thing>_section` (D10 Zig, D14 ObjC: enum `true`) for ELF AND PE: answer from the member's\n  section-name table (`.hcfg` literally; PE names are 8-byte NUL-padded), generic over `<thing>` (regex `has_(\\w+?)_section`).\n  Don't confuse with the many `__objc_*` sections on D14 -- only the literal name counts.\n- **Field set per old group** -- old groups gain ids over days (D8 padded every group to 10). Answer by field name from the\n  parsed facts dict of THAT member; an unknown field must log and fall through, never crash.\n- **Speed flags (no answer change)** -- the harness's per-case timings (e.g. \"4.11 s on single_solve\", D14) are often taken under\n  CPU contention from parallel solver-tests; measure isolated with `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py ...` before\n  optimising. Floor of the cumulative bundle = AES-CTR + inflate + sha256 of the 67 MB d08 Swift member (~0.35 s/set); real\n  runs: single 0.5 s, 5-set Mastery ~1.4 s pinned.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `evidence.zip`, \"AES Encrypted\" | `7z x -pinfected -y evidence.zip` (Python: `pyzipper`); `sha256sum *` for every `artifact_sha256_K` (K = archive order within the group) |\n| `readelf -h -S` hint, ELF header questions | `readelf -hSW`, `readelf -sW`; `readelf -x .huntress` / `readelf -p .huntress` for the custom-section marker |\n| \"constant returned by recover_code\" / `disassembly` | `objdump -d -M intel --no-show-raw-insn` around `<recover_code>`; capstone on the FUNC symbol's st_value..st_size bytes |\n| Stripped C build, no `.symtab` | answer the absence the question defines (`[]`/`none`); only as recon find the leaf `b8 imm32 c3` (`lib.binary.recover_return_constants`) |\n| C++ / \"mangled\" / \"vtable\" / \"RTTI\" | `nm -C` / `c++filt`; `_ZTV<class>` (vtable), `_ZTI`/`_ZTS` (typeinfo); the PE COFF symtab: `objdump -t file.exe` |\n| `PE32+` MinGW `.exe` | `objdump -t` (COFF symbols + string table), `pefile` (Machine, OPTIONAL_HEADER.Magic, sections incl. `.hcfg`) |\n| \"CLI metadata\", `.dll` + `runtimeconfig.json`, `BSJB` | `ilspycmd file.dll` or Python `dnfile`; config = `<PrivateImplementationDetails>` FieldRVA static array; `BSJB v4.0.30319` |\n| Go (\"build info, function names, file paths\") | `go version -m file`; `lib.binary.go_buildinfo` / `go_pclntab_funcs` (stripped names survive in `.gopclntab`) |\n| Rust (mangled `_R`/`_ZN..17h<hash>E`, panic strings) | `readelf -hS` + `HCFG` scan was enough on D5; `rustfilt` / `lib.binary.rustfilt` if symbols are asked |\n| `.jar` / \"constant pool\" | unzip the jar, `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF` Main-Class, `javap -v -p Main.class`; `ConstantValue: String` base64 config |\n| Kotlin fat jar (`kotlin/`, `X$fn$1 extends ContinuationImpl` with `int label`) | Parse the Main-Class first, skip `kotlin/`/`org/jetbrains/`. Coroutine \"state machine\" = `invokeSuspend` switching on `label` |\n| Swift ELF (`swift5_*` sections, `$s<len><Module>` symbols, 60+ MB static stdlib) | Never eager-parse symbols; regex `SENGR` base64 in `.rodata` (getter: `movabs rax,0xd0000000000001fc` → chars at X+0x20); `bin/swift-demangle` |\n| Nim ELF (`NimMain`, `TM__<hash>_N`, `<proc>__<mod>_u<N>`, `fatal.nim`) | Plain ELF; config literal = `u64 cap\\|0x40..` then chars (text = X+8); two raw `HCFG` decoys -> regex `SENGR`, crc-gate |\n| D ELF (`_D<len><module>...`, `_D2rt`/`_D4core`, `DMDH`) | Plain ELF; `decodeConfig()` returns a NUL-terminated base64 `SENGR...` literal in `.rodata` |\n| Free Pascal ELF (`FPC 3.2.2 ... x86_64 - Linux`, `.fpcdata`, static stripped) | Plain ELF; HCFG RAW in `.data` -- `grep -abo HCFG`, crc-gate, offset = the magic |\n| Crystal ELF (`Crystal:H`, Boehm `GC_malloc`, `*crystal*` symbols) | Plain ELF; base64 `SENGR...` String literal behind a 12-byte header (`type_id=1, bytesize, length`); offset = the `S` |\n| Objective-C ELF (`__objc_selectors`/`__objc_classes`/`__objc_cats`/`__objc_protocols` sections, `objc_msg_lookup_super`/`__objc_load` imports = GNUstep libobjc, `._OBJC_CLASS_<Name>`, `_i_<Class>__<sel>_` method symbols) | Plain ELF: readelf header ids as usual. HCFG RAW in its own `.hcfg` PROGBITS section (`readelf -x .hcfg`); `has_hcfg_section` = `true`. The ObjC class/selector \"persistence descriptor\" (`TriggerDescriptor initWithTrigger:`) was flavour, unasked. If ObjC metadata is ever asked: `readelf -sW \\| grep -E '_OBJC_CLASS_\\|objc_sel_name_'` |\n| Packed / high entropy / `UPX!` | `lib.binary.packer_info` → `upx -d` on a COPY (not seen yet) |\n| Real code-reversing question (not seen yet) | `rizin -q -c \"aaa; pdf @ sym.<fn>\"`; Ghidra headless `lib.binary.ghidra_decompile` (heavy, last resort) |\n\n## Day by day\n**D1 \"ELF Aware\"** (9 Qs; ~14 min, 4 wrong). C ELF64 header fields, `.huntress` marker, has_symtab, recover_code constant, entry;\nspellings learned by rejection. TT slot bundle: stripped profile and a renamed designated fn (→ `none`).\n**D2 \"Mangled\"** (17 Qs; ~22 min, 5 wrong). + C++ (ELF or MinGW PE32+); first HCFG (`.hcfg`). PE symbol fields want COMDAT\n`.text$<mangled>` / `.rdata$<mangled>` (all-or-nothing set POSTs hid this for hours).\n**D3 \"Table Manners\"** (24 Qs; ~1 h 48 min, ~60 wrong). + .NET 8 PE32 dll; FieldRVA HCFG. Format `pe_cli` after ~50 rejected synonyms.\n**D4 \"Go Fish\"** (32 Qs; ~1.5 min, 1 wrong). Static stripped Go ELF. `architecture` `amd64` REJECTED → `x86-64` (container's words).\n**D5 \"Rust Belt\"** (40 Qs; 7 s, 0 wrong). Static Rust ELF; D4 solver passed unchanged.\n**D6 \"Pool Party\"** (48 Qs; ~5 min, 1 wrong). `.jar` constant-pool base64 HCFG; new `hcfg_version`; `jar_jvm` REJECTED → `jar`.\nKeep nested .jar/.apk whole (recursive unzip lost the `d06--` prefix).\n**D7 \"Routine Check\"** (56 Qs; 3 min, 0 wrong). 5 MB Kotlin fat jar; scan the Main-Class first, not ~3300 runtime classes.\n**D8 \"Swift Justice\"** (80 Qs). 67 MB static Swift ELF; old groups backfilled to 10 ids. d08 elf_class/machine `kind: integer`\n→ `64`/`62`. Eager `pyelftools` symbols + headerless-XOR brute force cost 60 s+ each. Mastery set d01 was STRIPPED: answer `[]`\n/ `false` as the question defines -- the leaf-`mov eax` heuristic failed all 5 sets.\n**D9 \"Nimble\"** (90 Qs; 86 s, 0 wrong). Nim ELF; two raw `HCFG` decoys, real blob base64; NEW `hcfg_offset` 30696 = first base64 char.\n**D10 \"Zig Zag\"** (100 Qs; ~33 s, 0 wrong). Stripped Zig ELF, raw `.hcfg` section; NEW enum `has_hcfg_section` = `true`;\nMastery set2's d10 was a Zig PE (format `pe`).\n**D11 \"D-Day\"** (110 Qs; ~36 s, 0 wrong). DMD ELF, base64 HCFG in `.rodata`, hcfg_offset 368272; carried-over solver answered all.\n**D12 \"Pascal's Wager\"** (120 Qs; ~54 s, 2 wrong POSTs). FPC ELF, HCFG RAW in `.data` → hcfg_offset 82928 (the magic). The raw-scan\nbranch did not record its offset (`none`); bisect POSTs isolated d07-d12; patched → CORRECT. Every scan path fills every location field.\n**D13 \"Crystal Clear\"** (130 Qs; ~14 s, 0 wrong). Crystal ELF, base64 HCFG String literal, hcfg_offset 560188 (first char).\nTT 80 s / Mastery 3 sets 200 s, both first try.\n\n**D14 \"Selective Memory\"** (140 Qs; GM CORRECT 9 s after start, 0 wrong, carried-over solver, no worker reversing). Prompt:\n\"Objective-C never forgets: every class, every selector, every string is registered and waiting. Read the persistence\ndescriptor and learn what this binary remembers.\" New d14 = `d14--variant-000.elf`, 17,304 B Objective-C ELF64 x86-64 ET_EXEC,\ndynamic (GNUstep libobjc: `objc_msg_lookup_super`, `__objc_load`; `__objc_selectors`/`_classes`/`_cats`/`_protocols`/\n`_constant_string`/`_class_aliases` sections), not stripped, no `.comment`; one class `TriggerDescriptor`\n(`initWithTrigger:`, `triggerName`, `eventCountForModel:`).\n- d14 ids: sha256, architecture, format, machine, 5 config, `has_hcfg_section` -- no never-seen field (D10's field returned).\n- HCFG RAW in a dedicated read-only `.hcfg` PROGBITS section at file 0xfa0 (`HCFG 01 a1 6f01 da91f479` = ver 1, key 0xa1,\n  len 367, crc `0x79f491da`) → `BR14-000` / `node-000.day14.example.invalid`; `has_hcfg_section` `true`.\n- Confirmed again: format `elf` (exact_text), architecture/machine `x86-64` (pattern). The ObjC \"selectors / persistence\n  descriptor\" theme was not asked -- 9th day running that the language flavour is decoration.\n- TT 30 s window, in_window 2.42 s (BR14-002); Mastery 3 sets / 420 ids, 30 s window, in_window 6.01 s (BR14-002/007/004;\n  download 2.05 s + solve 2.82 s). Both CORRECT first try. Generalize worker: a speed flag only (contention), no code change.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n| Field family | Accepted form | Rejected (never resubmit) |\n|---|---|---|\n| elf_class (`kind` exact_text) | `ELF64` / `ELF32` (readelf style) | ELFCLASS64 |\n| elf_class (`kind: integer`, D8) | the bit width `64` / `32` | `2` / `1` (raw EI_CLASS byte) |\n| machine (`kind: integer`, D8-D9) | decimal e_machine (`62` = x86-64; u16 at offset 18 in EI_DATA order) | — |\n| endianness | `little` / `big` | little endian, lsb, msb |\n| machine (ELF) | `x86-64`, `x86`, `AArch64`, `ARM` | EM_X86_64, x86_64, amd64 |\n| machine (PE FILE_HEADER) | 0x14c → `i386`; 0x8664 → `x86-64` | x86 (for PE i386); raw `0x8664` |\n| architecture | the same machine words (Go ELF amd64 → `x86-64`; Go PE 0x8664 → `x86-64`) | amd64, arm64, 386, x86_64 |\n| elf_type | the constant `ET_EXEC` / `ET_DYN` | EXEC |\n| entry_point, crc32_hex, xor_key_hex | lowercase hex with `0x` (crc `0x%08x`, key `0x%02x`) | — |\n| recover_code | base-10 integer (`mov eax, 0x1fa4` → 8100); `none` if the named function is absent and the format allows it | the renamed function's constant |\n| has_symtab / has_cpp_* | enum `true`/`false` | — |\n| marker | exact `.huntress` string without the NUL; `none` if the section is missing | — |\n| format (native) | lowercase container: `elf`, `pe` (`macho` presumed) | ELF, ELF64, elf64-x86-64, HCFG, json, exe, pe32+, coff, mz |\n| format (.NET) | `pe_cli` | ~50 synonyms — lib/knowledge.py DOTNET_FORMAT_REJECTED |\n| format (Java/Kotlin jar) | `jar` (D6 Java, D7 Kotlin) | jar_jvm |\n| format / architecture (Swift, Nim, Zig, D, FPC, Crystal, ObjC ELF; D8-D14) | `elf` / `x86-64` (source language never changes the container label) | — |\n| C++ symbols (ELF) | bare Itanium mangled name (`_ZNK...`, `_ZTV...`) | the demangled form |\n| C++ symbols (PE/MinGW) | COMDAT section name `.text$<mangled>` (function), `.rdata$<mangled>` (vtable) | bare mangled name |\n| section_names (JSON) | pyelftools order INCLUDING the leading `\"\"` | list without \"\" |\n| symbols (JSON) | non-empty .symtab names, table order, dupes kept | list with the \"\" entries |\n| disassembly (JSON) | capstone intel `\"mov eax, 8100\"`, `\"ret\"`, decimal immediates | hex imm, `\"ret \"`, `mov eax,0x..` |\n| metadata_version | BSJB root string `v4.0.30319` | net8.0 / TFM / assembly version |\n| config_* | values verbatim from the decoded HCFG JSON (mutex keeps ONE backslash) | JSON-escaped `\\\\` |\n| hcfg_version | header byte 4 as a decimal integer | — |\n| has_hcfg_section (D10, D14, enum) | `true` when a section is literally named `.hcfg` (Zig ELF/PE, ObjC ELF) | — |\n| hcfg_offset (`kind: integer`, D9, D11-D13) | decimal FILE offset of the stored blob's first byte: base64 text start (`30696`, `368272`, `560188`), RAW = the `HCFG` magic (`82928`) | — (not tried: VA, struct start, `strings -t d` offset-1) |\n| xor_key_hex | HCFG header byte 5 as `0x%02x` | — |\n| compression_methods (jar, `kind: json`) | sorted distinct ZIP `compress_type` ids, compact: `[0,8]` | — |\nNaming law (from playbook.py): native format = container only; a managed .NET binary = container_runtime from the spec tokens (pe+cli).\nJava broke the compound law (`jar`), so when a label is new, try the plain container name AND the compound, one per POST.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **A multi-field POST is all-or-nothing.** One wrong field fails the set and hides which field was wrong (D2: correct `pe` looked\n  rejected for hours). Submit unconfirmed/new fields ALONE; batch only the known ones.\n- **Guessing synonyms for a synthetic label** (D3 .NET format: ~50 tries, ~1.5 h). Derive from spec tokens and the playbook naming laws,\n  use `hctf labels`, and read the question `syntax` first: the GM embeds hints.\n- **Chasing the prompt's theme** (D5-D14): the language flavour (selectors, protocols, coroutines, record layouts) has never been\n  asked since D4. Read the contract ids first; reverse only what an id asks for.\n- **Shell/JSON quoting** of `Global\\Huntress...` mutexes: build the submit JSON with python/jq, not by hand in a shell string.\n- **capstone `ret` has an empty op_str**: `f\"{m} {o}\"` gives `\"ret \"`. Strip it, and convert immediates to decimal.\n- **Cumulative zip**: old groups' answers carry over when their sha256 match; spend the time on the NEW group only.\n- **Recursive unzip** destroys nested containers (.jar/.apk) and their `dNN--` prefix; keep them whole.\n- **Same field name, different `kind`** (D8 elf_class/machine): read `answer_format.kind` per id.\n- **Huge members** (D8: 67 MB Swift): any per-key xor brute force or per-field re-parse blows a timed window. Cheap encodings first\n  (raw magic, base64 `SENGR`), crc-gate every hit, parse each member once.\n- **Decoy magics** (D9 Nim): code that CHECKS the magic embeds `\"HCFG\"` literals. Empty len 0 => crc32(b\"\")==0 passes! Require\n  non-empty JSON that parses, keep scanning, then try the base64 form.\n- **Location fields per scan path** (D12): a decoder with raw AND base64 branches must return the hit offset from BOTH. Before\n  submitting, assert no `none` where a config was decoded.\n- **`strings -t d` offsets on Nim/Swift literals**: a printable byte before the text shifts the offset by 1. Use `grep -abo` /\n  `re.finditer(...).start()` on the exact token.\n- **Jar members are deflated**: `grep HCFG file.jar` finds nothing. Inflate the class, read constant-pool strings, base64-decode.\n- **Stripped builds / renamed functions** in variants (D1 TT, D2 Mastery set2, D8 Mastery d01): answer what the question defines\n  for absence (`[]`, `none`, has_symtab=false); never substitute a heuristic constant.\n- **Speed flags measured under load** (D12, D14): \"N s on single_solve\" from a parallel solver-test is contention; re-measure\n  pinned and isolated before touching code.\n- **Tool parity**: ilspycmd, dotnet, rustfilt, GoReSym, rabin2, swift-demangle are in `bin/`; monodis/de4dot are not.\n- **Timed windows** (6-30 s; download is a big share of a 3-5 set Mastery): early TT/Mastery expiries were download/orchestration\n  latency, not solver speed. After editing hctf/*.py, restart the orchestrator (D1/D2 ran stale modules).\n- **PE machine map must include 0x8664 → `x86-64`**: a from-scratch replay once emitted `0x8664` and failed TT twice.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":4,"newStart":1,"newLines":4,"lines":["-# binary-reverse-engineering — technique log (days 1-13; updated after every day)","+# binary-reverse-engineering — technique log (days 1-14; updated after every day)"," "," How this lane has looked so far (OBSERVATIONS, not guarantees):"," - **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a"]},{"oldStart":8,"oldLines":47,"newStart":8,"newLines":47,"lines":["   D4 static stripped Go ELF, D5 static Rust ELF (debug_info), D6 Java .jar, D7 Kotlin fat .jar (5 MB, ~3300 entries), D8 Swift ELF","   (67 MB, static stdlib+Foundation+ICU, not stripped), D9 Nim ELF (60 KB, dynamic glibc, not stripped), D10 Zig ELF (134 KB,","   dynamic glibc, stripped, clang/LLD 19 zig-bootstrap in `.comment`) -- a Zig PE `.exe` in Mastery set2, D11 D-language ELF (1 MB,","-  DMD, druntime static + dynamic glibc, not stripped, debug_info), D12 Free Pascal ELF (100 KB, FPC 3.2.2, static, stripped), D13 Crystal ELF (749 KB, dynamic glibc + libgc, not","-  stripped).","+  DMD, druntime static + dynamic glibc, not stripped, debug_info), D12 Free Pascal ELF (100 KB, FPC 3.2.2, static, stripped), D13","+  Crystal ELF (749 KB, dynamic glibc + libgc, not stripped), D14 Objective-C ELF (17 KB, GNUstep libobjc ABI, dynamic, not stripped).","   Answer ids `dNN_artifact_sha256_K` / `dNN_analysis_<field>`."," - From Day 2 on, every new-day member carries the same embedded **HCFG** config blob: `'HCFG' | u8 ver | u8 xor_key | u16 len (LE) |","   u32 crc32 | xor'd JSON` (JSON at offset 12; crc32 is over the decoded plaintext). Only its storage location changes","-  (`.hcfg` section, .NET FieldRVA array, Go/Rust rodata, base64'd in a Java/Kotlin constant pool, base64 Swift String literal in","-  `.rodata` on D8, base64 Nim/D string literal in `.rodata` on D9/D11, RAW in FPC `.data` on D12, base64 Crystal String literal in `.rodata` on D13). Scan raw bytes for `HCFG` AND for its base64 form `SENGR...` (raw `HCFG` can also be a false hit inside code: check crc).","+  (`.hcfg` section on D2/D10/D14, .NET FieldRVA array, Go/Rust rodata, base64'd in a Java/Kotlin constant pool, base64 Swift/Nim/D/","+  Crystal String literal in `.rodata` on D8/D9/D11/D13, RAW in FPC `.data` on D12). Scan raw bytes for `HCFG` AND for its base64","+  form `SENGR...` (raw `HCFG` can also be a false hit inside code: check crc).","   The JSON also carries never-asked keys (ipv4, windows_path, linux_path, service, host_model on D7): parse the whole dict so a new `config_<key>` id is free."," - The analysis is easy (headers, symbols, one config blob). The hard part is the GM's exact label for a few `exact_text` fields (format,","-  machine, disassembly, symbol). The question set grows each day (9 → 17 → 24 → 32 → 40 → 48 → 56 → 80 → 90 → 100 → 110 → 120 → 130 fields); old groups reuse the same bytes,","-  but D8 BACKFILLED old groups to 10 ids each (new: has_symtab, has_cpp_typeinfo/vtable, xor_key_hex, hcfg_version, compression_methods).","-- The prompt's theme (Rust panics, D7 \"coroutine state machine\", D8 Swift \"protocols\", D9 Nim \"runtime fingerprints\") has NOT","-  been asked since D4: the new group gets sha256, format, config_campaign/domain/mutex/url/crc32_hex + 1-3 extra ids","-  (architecture D4-D5/D8-D12, hcfg_version D6-D7, elf_class/machine as INTEGERS D8-D9, `hcfg_offset` D9 + D11 + D12, `has_hcfg_section`","-  D10). D11/D12/D13 added NO new field (D12 = hcfg_offset on a RAW blob; D13 \"follow the DNS labels\" = just the","-  config domain/url). Usually exactly ONE","-  never-seen field per day: grep the new group's ids against the solver's field table before anything else.","-- Time Trial ≈ 6-16 s; Mastery = `setN.` prefixed copies, 2 sets (7-12 s) through D7, 5 sets / 400-450 ids / 20-27 s on D8-D9,","-  3 sets / 300-390 ids / 28-30 s on D10-D12 (TT 30 s too; D13 TT 80 s / Mastery 200 s); artifacts are named `delivery N: evidence.zip`.","+  machine, disassembly, symbol). The question set grows +10/day from D8 (80 → 90 → ... → 140 on D14); old groups reuse the same","+  bytes, but D8 BACKFILLED old groups to 10 ids each (new: has_symtab, has_cpp_typeinfo/vtable, xor_key_hex, hcfg_version, compression_methods).","+- **The prompt's language theme has NOT been asked since D4** (Rust panics, Kotlin \"state machine\", Swift \"protocols\", Nim","+  \"runtime fingerprints\", D \"templates\", Pascal \"record layouts\", Crystal \"DNS labels\", ObjC \"classes/selectors/persistence","+  descriptor\"). The new group gets sha256, format, architecture, machine, config_campaign/domain/mutex/url/crc32_hex + ONE","+  rotating extra id from a small pool: hcfg_version (D6-D7), `hcfg_offset` (D9, D11-D13), `has_hcfg_section` (D10, D14),","+  elf_class/machine as INTEGERS (D8-D9). D11-D14 introduced NO never-seen field: grep the new group's ids against the solver's","+  field table before anything else; if all are known, run the carried-over solver and submit.","+- Time Trial ≈ 6-16 s early; Mastery = `setN.` prefixed copies, 2 sets through D7, 5 sets / 400-450 ids on D8-D9, 3 sets / 300-420","+  ids on D10-D14 (TT 30 s; D13 TT 80 s / Mastery 200 s; D14 both 30 s); artifacts are named `delivery N: evidence.zip`."," - **D10 RELAXED the label fields**: 36 ids are now `kind: pattern` whose syntax ACCEPTS equivalents (format: \"ELF or PE; case,","   ELF32/ELF64/PE32/PE32+ accepted\"; machine/architecture: \"standard tool or symbolic label, or decimal/hex code\"; e_type and","   endianness: symbolic constant / readelf label / numeric code; .NET format: any container_runtime token with CLI/CLR/.NET). D8-D9's","   integer machine became pattern. Keep emitting the GM-confirmed spellings; the old REJECTED lists may be stale for pattern ids.","+  (D14: `dNN_analysis_format` is still `exact_text` -> `elf`.)"," "," ## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)"," - **HCFG location / encoding** -- same blob, different storage per container (`.hcfg` section, .NET FieldRVA, Go/Rust rodata,","-  base64 inside a Java/Kotlin constant pool, base64 Swift/Nim string literal in ELF `.rodata` on D8/D9): scan raw bytes for `HCFG`","-  and for `SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]*=*` (base64 of `HCFG`, std or urlsafe), decode, accept only if crc32(plain) matches AND the JSON","-  parses -- keep scanning past a failing hit (D9 Nim had two raw `HCFG` decoys); never a fixed offset.","-- **Location-as-answer (`hcfg_offset`, D9/D11/D12)** -- base-10 FILE offset of the first byte of the stored blob as it sits in","-  the member: base64 form -> the `S` of `SENGR...` (D9 Nim 30696, D11 D 368272, D13 Crystal 560188 -- the text, not the String header 12 B before it); RAW form -> the `H` of `HCFG` (D12 FPC 82928 =","-  0x143f0 in `.data`, GM-confirmed single+TT+Mastery x3). Constant across a day's variants although shas differ -- still","-  compute it: record `m.start()` of whichever scan hit (raw OR base64) validated, on BOTH paths (D12's raw path returned `none`).","-- **Any other storage encoding -> `lib.binary.hcfg_scan(data, deadline=None)`** (Day 14 prep; pure stdlib, Homebase-safe,","-  ~15 ms / 2 MB, ~30 ms / 4 MB real ELF, ~0.6 s / 67 MB). Returns every `HcfgHit` (offset, encoding, version, key, length, crc,","-  crc_ok, config, plain, speculative, detail) best first; take `lib.binary.hcfg_find(data)` (first crc-valid + JSON-parsing hit).","-  Covers raw, base64 (std / url / newline-wrapped), hex (plain, `48 43`, `48:43`, `\\x48`, `0x48, `), base32 (upper/lower),","-  base85, ascii85 (`<~` optional), UTF-16LE/BE of raw/base64/hex/base32/base85, reversed raw, reversed base64, single-byte","-  xor'd base64 / xor'd raw (key-independent xor-diff search), zlib, gzip, raw deflate (fixed-Huffman anchor anywhere; headerless","-  dynamic brute force only while nothing valid was found and the file is <= 1 MiB, `HCTF_HCFG_DEFLATE_MAX`). Decoys (bad crc,","-  truncated, bare `\"HCFG\"` strings, wrong magic) come back with `valid=False`. Offset convention per encoding (`hcfg_offset`):","+  base64 inside a Java/Kotlin constant pool, base64 Swift/Nim/D/Crystal string literal in ELF `.rodata`, raw FPC `.data`): scan raw","+  bytes for `HCFG` and for `SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]*=*` (base64 of `HCFG`, std or urlsafe), decode, accept only if crc32(plain)","+  matches AND the JSON parses -- keep scanning past a failing hit (D9 Nim had two raw `HCFG` decoys); never a fixed offset.","+  Storage did NOT change across a day's variants on any day so far (D14 `.hcfg` at file 0xfa0 in single/TT/all 3 sets).","+- **Location-as-answer (`hcfg_offset`, D9/D11-D13)** -- base-10 FILE offset of the first byte of the stored blob as it sits in","+  the member: base64 form -> the `S` of `SENGR...` (D9 Nim 30696, D11 D 368272, D13 Crystal 560188 -- the text, not the String","+  header 12 B before it); RAW form -> the `H` of `HCFG` (D12 FPC 82928). Constant across a day's variants although shas differ --","+  still compute it: record `m.start()` of whichever scan hit (raw OR base64) validated, on BOTH paths (D12's raw path returned `none`).","+- **Any other storage encoding -> `lib.binary.hcfg_scan(data, deadline=None)`** (pure stdlib, ~15 ms / 2 MB, ~0.6 s / 67 MB).","+  Returns every `HcfgHit` (offset, encoding, version, key, length, crc, crc_ok, config, plain, speculative, detail) best first;","+  take `lib.binary.hcfg_find(data)` (first crc-valid + JSON-parsing hit). Covers raw, base64 (std/url/wrapped), hex (plain, `48 43`,","+  `48:43`, `\\x48`, `0x48, `), base32, base85, ascii85, UTF-16LE/BE of those, reversed raw/base64, single-byte xor'd base64/raw,","+  zlib, gzip, raw deflate. Decoys come back `valid=False`. Offset convention per encoding (`hcfg_offset`):"," ","   | encoding | offset = | status |","   |---|---|---|"]},{"oldStart":57,"oldLines":34,"newStart":57,"newLines":35,"lines":["   | base64url, base32, base85, hex, hex-sep | first char of the stored text (`\\` of `\\x48`, `0` of `0x48`) | speculative |","   | ascii85 | the `<` of `<~` if present, else first char | speculative |","   | utf16le-* / utf16be-* | first byte of the first code unit (BE: its `00`); LE/BE tie -> the 2-aligned reading, else LE | speculative |","-  | reversed-raw / reversed-base64 | lowest file offset of the reversed region (where the blob's LAST byte / the `=` pad sits) | speculative |","+  | reversed-raw / reversed-base64 | lowest file offset of the reversed region | speculative |","   | xor-base64 / xor-raw | first stored byte (`detail` = `xor=0x..`) | speculative |","-  | zlib / gzip / deflate | first byte of the compressed stream (`78`, `1f 8b`, the deflate block header) | speculative |","+  | zlib / gzip / deflate | first byte of the compressed stream | speculative |"," ","-  Wired into the newest binary solver (D13 `native_hcfg` + `jar_hcfg`): runs only when the D13 scan finds nothing, or when its","-  hit parses but fails crc32 (then a crc-valid blob elsewhere wins). Kill switch `HCTF_HCFG_SCAN_EXT=0` = the D13 behaviour","-  exactly. A speculative offset is a first guess: if the GM rejects it, try the offset of the container header in front of","-  the stored form (String header, length prefix, `<~` / quote) next. Fixtures: `tests/data/hcfg_fixtures/` (`make.py`); checks in","-  `tests/test_day14_s4.py`.","-- **xor key / config values** -- re-roll per variant; derive from the header byte, never from the sample.","+  Wired into the binary solver as a fallback (kill switch `HCTF_HCFG_SCAN_EXT=0`); not needed on D14. A speculative offset is a","+  first guess: if rejected, try the offset of the container header in front of the stored form next. Fixtures: `tests/data/hcfg_fixtures/`.","+- **xor key / config values** -- re-roll per variant (`BRNN-00V`, `node-00V.dayNN...`, crc); derive from the header byte, never","+  from the sample. D13 key = 0x91+N; D14 single BR14-000 key 0xa1, TT BR14-002, Mastery BR14-002/007/004."," - **Container per member** -- ELF vs PE32+ `.exe` re-rolls per member: Mastery set2 had d02 C++ as `.exe` (D3-D5, D7, D10) and d04","-  Go as `.exe` (D4, D5, D7, D10); D6 set2 had both as ELF; D10 set2 had the NEW d10 Zig member as a PE too (format `pe`). Labels come from the header of THIS member (Go PE: format `pe`, architecture `x86-64` from Machine).","-- **Variant index per group** -- `dNN--variant-XXX` re-rolls per group and mode (D7 TT: d03-001, d04-006, d07-005 ...); sizes","-  and config values change, names/layout don't. TT == Mastery set1 bytes on D7; D8 TT re-used the D7 TT old-group indices","-  (d08 = variant-000); D9 TT == set1 for d02-d09 (d09 BR09-003) but d01 differed (TT variant-000 `8100`, all 5 Mastery sets one","-  other d01 with `mov eax, 8104`, symtab present). Mastery d09 = BR09-003/006/001/004/007; d08 stayed variant-000..004.","+  Go as `.exe` (D4, D5, D7, D10); D10 set2 had the NEW d10 Zig member as a PE too (format `pe`). Labels come from the header of","+  THIS member (Go PE: format `pe`, architecture `x86-64` from Machine).","+- **Variant index per group** -- `dNN--variant-XXX` re-rolls per group and mode; sizes and config values change, names/layout","+  don't. TT often == Mastery set1 bytes (D7, D9, D14: TT and set1 both BR14-002); a carry-over d01 can differ (D9 Mastery d01","+  `mov eax, 8104`). Pair members by sha256, never by index."," - **Mastery packaging** -- `setN.` prefixed ids, each set its own `delivery N: evidence.zip` (same filename): pair by sha256.","-  Set count re-rolls: 2 (D2-D7), 5 on D8-D9 (set2/set4 had d02/d04 as PE both days), 3 on D10: loop over every `setN.`. From D9 (all","-  lanes) the first question of each set ends `Evidence case: d09-m-<16hex>. [assigned-artifact-sha256:<zip sha256>]`","-  (TT: `d09-tt-...`): an explicit set -> delivery map; it is question TEXT, never part of an answer.","+  Set count re-rolls: 2 (D2-D7), 5 (D8-D9), 3 (D10-D14): loop over every `setN.`. From D9 the first question of each set ends","+  `Evidence case: dNN-m-<16hex>. [assigned-artifact-sha256:<zip sha256>]` (TT: `dNN-tt-...`): an explicit set -> delivery map;","+  it is question TEXT, never part of an answer."," - **answer_format.kind for the same field name** -- D8: `d01_analysis_elf_class`/`machine` exact_text (`ELF64`/`x86-64`) and","-  `d08_analysis_elf_class`/`machine` integer (`64`/`62`) in ONE contract; D9 `d09_analysis_machine` integer again. Rule:","-  dispatch on `kind`, not on the field name.","-- **Feature-presence fields** -- `has_<thing>_section` (D10 `has_hcfg_section`, enum true/false) for ELF AND PE: answer from the","-  member's section-name table (`.hcfg` literally; PE names are 8-byte NUL-padded), generic over `<thing>` (regex `has_(\\w+?)_section`).","+  `d08_analysis_elf_class`/`machine` integer (`64`/`62`) in ONE contract. Rule: dispatch on `kind`, not on the field name.","+- **Feature-presence fields** -- `has_<thing>_section` (D10 Zig, D14 ObjC: enum `true`) for ELF AND PE: answer from the member's","+  section-name table (`.hcfg` literally; PE names are 8-byte NUL-padded), generic over `<thing>` (regex `has_(\\w+?)_section`).","+  Don't confuse with the many `__objc_*` sections on D14 -- only the literal name counts."," - **Field set per old group** -- old groups gain ids over days (D8 padded every group to 10). Answer by field name from the","-  parsed facts dict of THAT member; an unknown field must log and fall through, never crash. Keep the older 56/112-id cases passing.","-  D9 kept D8's 10 ids for d01-d08 (d08: sha, architecture, elf_class, format, machine, 5 config) and added d09 with `hcfg_offset`.","+  parsed facts dict of THAT member; an unknown field must log and fall through, never crash.","+- **Speed flags (no answer change)** -- the harness's per-case timings (e.g. \"4.11 s on single_solve\", D14) are often taken under","+  CPU contention from parallel solver-tests; measure isolated with `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py ...` before","+  optimising. Floor of the cumulative bundle = AES-CTR + inflate + sha256 of the 67 MB d08 Swift member (~0.35 s/set); real","+  runs: single 0.5 s, 5-set Mastery ~1.4 s pinned."," "," ## Recognition cues -> first move"," | You see | First move |"]},{"oldStart":92,"oldLines":149,"newStart":93,"newLines":120,"lines":[" | `evidence.zip`, \"AES Encrypted\" | `7z x -pinfected -y evidence.zip` (Python: `pyzipper`); `sha256sum *` for every `artifact_sha256_K` (K = archive order within the group) |"," | `readelf -h -S` hint, ELF header questions | `readelf -hSW`, `readelf -sW`; `readelf -x .huntress` / `readelf -p .huntress` for the custom-section marker |"," | \"constant returned by recover_code\" / `disassembly` | `objdump -d -M intel --no-show-raw-insn` around `<recover_code>`; capstone on the FUNC symbol's st_value..st_size bytes |","-| Stripped C build, no `.symtab` | find the leaf `b8 imm32 c3` (`mov eax, imm; ret`) in `.text` (`lib.binary.recover_return_constants`) and check it against what `main` inlines |","-| C++ / \"mangled\" / \"vtable\" / \"RTTI\" | `nm -C` / `c++filt`; look for `_ZTV<class>` (vtable), `_ZTI`/`_ZTS` (typeinfo), `_ZNK<cls>5scoreEPKc`; the PE COFF symtab: `objdump -t file.exe` |","+| Stripped C build, no `.symtab` | answer the absence the question defines (`[]`/`none`); only as recon find the leaf `b8 imm32 c3` (`lib.binary.recover_return_constants`) |","+| C++ / \"mangled\" / \"vtable\" / \"RTTI\" | `nm -C` / `c++filt`; `_ZTV<class>` (vtable), `_ZTI`/`_ZTS` (typeinfo); the PE COFF symtab: `objdump -t file.exe` |"," | `PE32+` MinGW `.exe` | `objdump -t` (COFF symbols + string table), `pefile` (Machine, OPTIONAL_HEADER.Magic, sections incl. `.hcfg`) |","-| \"CLI metadata\", `.dll` + `runtimeconfig.json`, `BSJB` in strings | `ilspycmd file.dll` (decompile to C#; installed 2026-10-07) or Python `dnfile`; config = `<PrivateImplementationDetails>` FieldRVA static array; `strings` shows `BSJB v4.0.30319` |","-| Go (\"build info, function names, file paths\") | `go version -m file` (buildinfo: go1.x, GOARCH); `lib.binary.go_buildinfo` / `go_pclntab_funcs` (stripped names survive in `.gopclntab`) |","-| Rust (\"mangled symbols with a distinct accent\", panic strings) | `readelf -hS` + `HCFG` scan was enough on D5; demangle with `rustfilt` (installed) or `lib.binary.rustfilt` (binary) if symbols are asked |","-| `.jar` / \"constant pool\" | unzip the jar, read `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF` Main-Class, `javap -v -p Main.class`; look for `ConstantValue: String` (`static final String CONFIG`) |","-| Kotlin fat jar (`kotlin/` runtime, `META-INF/main.kotlin_module`, `X$fn$1 extends ContinuationImpl` with `int label`) | Same as `.jar`: parse the Main-Class first, skip `kotlin/`/`org/jetbrains/`. Coroutine \"state machine\" = `invokeSuspend` switching on `label`; branch logic is plain `javap -c` (`lookupswitch` on String.hashCode + `ldc` results) |","-| Swift ELF (`swift5_*` sections, `$s<len><Module>...` symbols, clang `swiftlang` in `.comment`, huge 60+ MB static stdlib) | `nm FILE \\| grep '\\$s[0-9]*<Module>'` (app symbols sit just after `frame_dummy`); `bin/swift-demangle`; config getter = `lea rax,[rip+X]; movabs rax,0xd0000000000001fc; ret` → literal chars at X+0x20, count = low 48 bits (0x1fc); or simply regex `SENGR` base64 |","-| Nim ELF (`NimMain`/`NimMainModule`/`PreMain`, `TM__<hash>_N` literals, `<proc>__<mod>_u<N>` mangling e.g. `encodedConfig__v000_u31`, `@m..@snim@slib@s...nim.c` / `fatal.nim` strings, `nimZeroMem`/`nimCopyMem`) | It is plain C-compiled ELF: header ids via readelf as usual. Config proc returns a string literal: `mov eax,0x1fc; lea rdx,[rip+X]` (len, `TM__` ptr); the literal is `u64 cap\\|0x4000000000000000` then the chars, so text = X+8 (file off = VA - segment base). Or regex `SENGR` |","-| D ELF (`_D<len><module>...` mangling e.g. `_D4v00012decodeConfigFZAya`, `_D2rt`/`_D4core` druntime symbols, `DMDH`/`DMDI` strings, no `.comment`) | Plain native ELF: readelf header ids as usual. Config = `decodeConfig()` returning a D string (`Aya` = immutable(char)[]); the base64 `SENGR...` literal is NUL-terminated in `.rodata` -- regex it. `evaluate`/`campaign` funcs exist but were never asked |","-| Free Pascal ELF (`FPC 3.2.2 [...] for x86_64 - Linux` string, `.fpcdata` section, static + stripped, `FPC_`/`fpc_` RTL names in strings) | Plain native ELF: readelf header ids as usual. HCFG sits RAW (magic + header + XOR'd JSON) in `.data` -- `grep -abo HCFG`, crc-gate, offset = the magic's offset. Pascal \"record layouts\" flavour unasked |","-| Crystal ELF (`Crystal:H` strings, Boehm GC exports `GC_malloc`/`GC_world_stopped`, `*crystal*` symbols via `nm`) | Plain native ELF: readelf header ids as usual. Config = base64 `SENGR...` Crystal String literal in `.rodata` behind a 12-byte header (`u32 type_id=1, u32 bytesize, u32 length`) -- regex it; offset = the `S`. \"DNS labels\" = the config's domain/url, no DNS wire format anywhere |","+| \"CLI metadata\", `.dll` + `runtimeconfig.json`, `BSJB` | `ilspycmd file.dll` or Python `dnfile`; config = `<PrivateImplementationDetails>` FieldRVA static array; `BSJB v4.0.30319` |","+| Go (\"build info, function names, file paths\") | `go version -m file`; `lib.binary.go_buildinfo` / `go_pclntab_funcs` (stripped names survive in `.gopclntab`) |","+| Rust (mangled `_R`/`_ZN..17h<hash>E`, panic strings) | `readelf -hS` + `HCFG` scan was enough on D5; `rustfilt` / `lib.binary.rustfilt` if symbols are asked |","+| `.jar` / \"constant pool\" | unzip the jar, `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF` Main-Class, `javap -v -p Main.class`; `ConstantValue: String` base64 config |","+| Kotlin fat jar (`kotlin/`, `X$fn$1 extends ContinuationImpl` with `int label`) | Parse the Main-Class first, skip `kotlin/`/`org/jetbrains/`. Coroutine \"state machine\" = `invokeSuspend` switching on `label` |","+| Swift ELF (`swift5_*` sections, `$s<len><Module>` symbols, 60+ MB static stdlib) | Never eager-parse symbols; regex `SENGR` base64 in `.rodata` (getter: `movabs rax,0xd0000000000001fc` → chars at X+0x20); `bin/swift-demangle` |","+| Nim ELF (`NimMain`, `TM__<hash>_N`, `<proc>__<mod>_u<N>`, `fatal.nim`) | Plain ELF; config literal = `u64 cap\\|0x40..` then chars (text = X+8); two raw `HCFG` decoys -> regex `SENGR`, crc-gate |","+| D ELF (`_D<len><module>...`, `_D2rt`/`_D4core`, `DMDH`) | Plain ELF; `decodeConfig()` returns a NUL-terminated base64 `SENGR...` literal in `.rodata` |","+| Free Pascal ELF (`FPC 3.2.2 ... x86_64 - Linux`, `.fpcdata`, static stripped) | Plain ELF; HCFG RAW in `.data` -- `grep -abo HCFG`, crc-gate, offset = the magic |","+| Crystal ELF (`Crystal:H`, Boehm `GC_malloc`, `*crystal*` symbols) | Plain ELF; base64 `SENGR...` String literal behind a 12-byte header (`type_id=1, bytesize, length`); offset = the `S` |","+| Objective-C ELF (`__objc_selectors`/`__objc_classes`/`__objc_cats`/`__objc_protocols` sections, `objc_msg_lookup_super`/`__objc_load` imports = GNUstep libobjc, `._OBJC_CLASS_<Name>`, `_i_<Class>__<sel>_` method symbols) | Plain ELF: readelf header ids as usual. HCFG RAW in its own `.hcfg` PROGBITS section (`readelf -x .hcfg`); `has_hcfg_section` = `true`. The ObjC class/selector \"persistence descriptor\" (`TriggerDescriptor initWithTrigger:`) was flavour, unasked. If ObjC metadata is ever asked: `readelf -sW \\| grep -E '_OBJC_CLASS_\\|objc_sel_name_'` |"," | Packed / high entropy / `UPX!` | `lib.binary.packer_info` → `upx -d` on a COPY (not seen yet) |"," | Real code-reversing question (not seen yet) | `rizin -q -c \"aaa; pdf @ sym.<fn>\"`; Ghidra headless `lib.binary.ghidra_decompile` (heavy, last resort) |"," "," ## Day by day","-**D1 \"ELF Aware\"** (9 Qs; ~14 min, 4 wrong). C ELF64: class, endianness, machine, e_type, `.huntress` marker, has_symtab,","-recover_code constant, entry point (readelf/objdump; pyelftools + capstone). Spellings learned by rejection. TT \"slot\" bundle","-(`slotN_<qid>`): stripped profile and a renamed designated fn (→ `none`, unconfirmed).","+**D1 \"ELF Aware\"** (9 Qs; ~14 min, 4 wrong). C ELF64 header fields, `.huntress` marker, has_symtab, recover_code constant, entry;","+spellings learned by rejection. TT slot bundle: stripped profile and a renamed designated fn (→ `none`).","+**D2 \"Mangled\"** (17 Qs; ~22 min, 5 wrong). + C++ (ELF or MinGW PE32+); first HCFG (`.hcfg`). PE symbol fields want COMDAT","+`.text$<mangled>` / `.rdata$<mangled>` (all-or-nothing set POSTs hid this for hours).","+**D3 \"Table Manners\"** (24 Qs; ~1 h 48 min, ~60 wrong). + .NET 8 PE32 dll; FieldRVA HCFG. Format `pe_cli` after ~50 rejected synonyms.","+**D4 \"Go Fish\"** (32 Qs; ~1.5 min, 1 wrong). Static stripped Go ELF. `architecture` `amd64` REJECTED → `x86-64` (container's words).","+**D5 \"Rust Belt\"** (40 Qs; 7 s, 0 wrong). Static Rust ELF; D4 solver passed unchanged.","+**D6 \"Pool Party\"** (48 Qs; ~5 min, 1 wrong). `.jar` constant-pool base64 HCFG; new `hcfg_version`; `jar_jvm` REJECTED → `jar`.","+Keep nested .jar/.apk whole (recursive unzip lost the `d06--` prefix).","+**D7 \"Routine Check\"** (56 Qs; 3 min, 0 wrong). 5 MB Kotlin fat jar; scan the Main-Class first, not ~3300 runtime classes.","+**D8 \"Swift Justice\"** (80 Qs). 67 MB static Swift ELF; old groups backfilled to 10 ids. d08 elf_class/machine `kind: integer`","+→ `64`/`62`. Eager `pyelftools` symbols + headerless-XOR brute force cost 60 s+ each. Mastery set d01 was STRIPPED: answer `[]`","+/ `false` as the question defines -- the leaf-`mov eax` heuristic failed all 5 sets.","+**D9 \"Nimble\"** (90 Qs; 86 s, 0 wrong). Nim ELF; two raw `HCFG` decoys, real blob base64; NEW `hcfg_offset` 30696 = first base64 char.","+**D10 \"Zig Zag\"** (100 Qs; ~33 s, 0 wrong). Stripped Zig ELF, raw `.hcfg` section; NEW enum `has_hcfg_section` = `true`;","+Mastery set2's d10 was a Zig PE (format `pe`).","+**D11 \"D-Day\"** (110 Qs; ~36 s, 0 wrong). DMD ELF, base64 HCFG in `.rodata`, hcfg_offset 368272; carried-over solver answered all.","+**D12 \"Pascal's Wager\"** (120 Qs; ~54 s, 2 wrong POSTs). FPC ELF, HCFG RAW in `.data` → hcfg_offset 82928 (the magic). The raw-scan","+branch did not record its offset (`none`); bisect POSTs isolated d07-d12; patched → CORRECT. Every scan path fills every location field.","+**D13 \"Crystal Clear\"** (130 Qs; ~14 s, 0 wrong). Crystal ELF, base64 HCFG String literal, hcfg_offset 560188 (first char).","+TT 80 s / Mastery 3 sets 200 s, both first try."," ","-**D2 \"Mangled\"** (17 Qs; ~22 min, 5 wrong). + C++ (ELF or MinGW PE32+). First HCFG (`.hcfg` section). vtable = `_ZTV<class owning","-score>`; PE symbol fields want COMDAT `.text$<mangled>` / `.rdata$<mangled>` (all-or-nothing set POSTs hid this for hours).","+**D14 \"Selective Memory\"** (140 Qs; GM CORRECT 9 s after start, 0 wrong, carried-over solver, no worker reversing). Prompt:","+\"Objective-C never forgets: every class, every selector, every string is registered and waiting. Read the persistence","+descriptor and learn what this binary remembers.\" New d14 = `d14--variant-000.elf`, 17,304 B Objective-C ELF64 x86-64 ET_EXEC,","+dynamic (GNUstep libobjc: `objc_msg_lookup_super`, `__objc_load`; `__objc_selectors`/`_classes`/`_cats`/`_protocols`/","+`_constant_string`/`_class_aliases` sections), not stripped, no `.comment`; one class `TriggerDescriptor`","+(`initWithTrigger:`, `triggerName`, `eventCountForModel:`).","+- d14 ids: sha256, architecture, format, machine, 5 config, `has_hcfg_section` -- no never-seen field (D10's field returned).","+- HCFG RAW in a dedicated read-only `.hcfg` PROGBITS section at file 0xfa0 (`HCFG 01 a1 6f01 da91f479` = ver 1, key 0xa1,","+  len 367, crc `0x79f491da`) → `BR14-000` / `node-000.day14.example.invalid`; `has_hcfg_section` `true`.","+- Confirmed again: format `elf` (exact_text), architecture/machine `x86-64` (pattern). The ObjC \"selectors / persistence","+  descriptor\" theme was not asked -- 9th day running that the language flavour is decoration.","+- TT 30 s window, in_window 2.42 s (BR14-002); Mastery 3 sets / 420 ids, 30 s window, in_window 6.01 s (BR14-002/007/004;","+  download 2.05 s + solve 2.82 s). Both CORRECT first try. Generalize worker: a speed flag only (contention), no code change."," ","-**D3 \"Table Manners\"** (24 Qs; ~1 h 48 min, ~60 wrong). + .NET 8 PE32 i386 dll: `dnfile` → BSJB `v4.0.30319`, FieldRVA HCFG.","-`d03_analysis_format` = `pe_cli` after ~50 rejected synonyms: compose labels from spec tokens.","-","-**D4 \"Go Fish\"** (32 Qs; ~1.5 min, 1 wrong). Static stripped Go ELF; HCFG in rodata. `architecture` `amd64` (GOARCH) REJECTED →","-`x86-64`: \"architecture\" uses the container's machine words, not the toolchain token.","-","-**D5 \"Rust Belt\"** (40 Qs; 7 s, 0 wrong, no LLM). Static Rust ELF; the D4 solver passed unchanged. Rust theme never asked.","-","-**D6 \"Pool Party\"** (48 Qs; ~5 min, 1 wrong). `.jar`: Main-Class `javap -v -p` → `static final String CONFIG` base64 → HCFG. New","-`hcfg_version` (byte 4, base-10). Format `jar_jvm` REJECTED → `jar`. Keep nested .jar/.apk members whole (recursive unzip lost the","-`d06--` prefix). Question texts got rewritten to name accepted spellings: read each `syntax`.","-","-**D7 \"Routine Check\"** (56 Qs; 3 min, 0 wrong). 5 MB Kotlin fat jar, same constant-pool base64 HCFG; scan the Main-Class first","-(not ~3300 runtime classes). Unasked \"state machine\": `evaluate()` lookupswitch on env `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`.","-","-**D8 \"Swift Justice\"** (80 Qs). New d08 = 67 MB static Swift ELF (~290k symbols, not stripped); old groups backfilled to 10 ids.","-- **Read `answer_format.kind` first:** d08 elf_class/machine were `integer` → bit width `64` (not EI_CLASS `2`) and `62`.","-- Eager `pyelftools` `iter_symbols()` and the headerless-XOR brute force each took 60 s+ on it (worker lost 120 s + a 66 s","-  profile). Recon with `readelf`/`nm`/`strings`; config = base64 HCFG in `.rodata` (`strings -n 40 | grep -m3 '^SENGR'`).","-- Mastery: 5 deliveries x ~31 MB; download ~4.6-10 s + solve ~8 s inside a 27 s window.","-- **Mastery mutated a carry-over ELF:** a STRIPPED d01 (no .symtab). The question says \"If that symbol is absent, submit []\";","-  the old \"last `mov eax, imm32; ret` leaf\" fallback answered `[\"mov eax, 8102\",\"ret\"]` and failed all 5 sets. Absent →","-  `[]`, has_symtab `false`, symbols `[]`. Never substitute a heuristic for an absence the question defines.","-- LIB: `lib.elf.fields(data)[1]` returns `elf_class_int`/`machine_int` for `kind == \"integer\"`.","-","-**D9 \"Nimble\"** (90 Qs; 86 s, 0 wrong). 60 KB Nim ELF (`.symtab` kept). Two raw `HCFG` DECOYS (assert text + magic-check","-literal) -> the real blob is base64 `SENGR...` in a Nim literal (8-byte cap header before the text). NEW `hcfg_offset` = 30696 =","-first base64 char. Lost: a jq `.answer_id` (contract questions use `.id`). TT 10 s / Mastery 5 sets 20 s, both first try.","-","-**D10 \"Zig Zag\"** (100 Qs; ~33 s, 0 wrong). 134 KB stripped Zig ELF; HCFG raw in a writable `.hcfg` section. NEW enum","-`has_hcfg_section` = `true` (generic `has_(\\w+?)_section` over section names, ELF and PE). \"ELF and PE side by side\" only meant","-Mastery set2's d10 was a Zig PE (format `pe`). TT in_window 2.85 s, Mastery 3 sets 5.59 s.","-","-**D11 \"D-Day\"** (110 Qs; ~36 s, 0 wrong). 1 MB DMD ELF; base64 HCFG NUL-terminated in `.rodata` after `.debug_line\\0`,","-hcfg_offset 368272. Carried-over solver answered everything (2 tool calls); \"template expansions\" flavour unasked.","-","-**D12 \"Pascal's Wager\"** (120 Qs; ~54 s start->CORRECT, 2 wrong POSTs). Prompt: \"Pascal is betting you won't read its record","-layouts ... read the configuration straight from memory's own filing cabinet.\" New d12 = `d12--variant-000.elf`, 100,976 B Free","-Pascal 3.2.2 ELF64 x86-64, static, stripped. d12 ids: sha, architecture, format, machine, 5 config, hcfg_offset (no new field).","-- HCFG RAW in `.data` at file offset 0x143f0 (`HCFG 01 81 7001 f881fce4` = ver 1, key 0x81, len 368) -> `hcfg_offset` **82928**","-  (offset of the magic itself); config `BR12-000` / `node-000.day12.example.invalid` / crc `0xe4fc81f8`.","-- The copied D11 solver decoded the raw blob but its raw-scan branch did not record the offset -> `none`. POST 1 (120 ids)","-  incorrect; the harness bisect POSTed d01-d06 (accepted) then d07-d12 (incorrect); worker `xxd -s 82900`, patched the raw","-  branch to return its offset (+ keep scanning past a raw decoy whose crc fails), CORRECT. Lesson: every scan path must","-  fill every location field.","-- TT 30 s window, in_window 2.9 s (BR12-004); Mastery 3 sets / 360 ids, in_window 5.14 s (BR12-004/005/006, offset 82928 in","-  all). Both CORRECT first try.","-","-**D13 \"Crystal Clear\"** (130 Qs; ~14 s start->CORRECT, 0 wrong, no worker tool call). Prompt: \"Crystal compiles to native code","-with a distinctive shine. Fingerprint the runtime, then follow the DNS labels\". New d13 = `d13--variant-000.elf`, 749,208 B","-Crystal ELF64 x86-64 (dynamic, libgc, symtab). d13 ids: sha, architecture, machine, format, 5 config, hcfg_offset (no new field).","-- Base64 HCFG in a Crystal String literal (`01000000 fc010000 fc010000` header, 508 chars) -> `hcfg_offset` **560188** (0x88c3c,","-  first base64 char); `BR13-000` / `node-000.day13.example.invalid` / crc `0xa69b7e61`, key 0x91. Domain never in plaintext.","-- The carried-over solver's `SENGR` regex + `m.start()` answered every field. TT (80 s window) in_window 2.41 s; Mastery 3 sets /","-  390 ids in_window 5.99 s (variants 007/002/005; key = 0x91+N; offset constant). Both CORRECT first try.","-"," ## GM answer conventions learned"," | Field family | Accepted form | Rejected (never resubmit) |"," |---|---|---|","-| elf_class (`answer_format.kind` exact_text) | `ELF64` / `ELF32` (readelf style) | ELFCLASS64 |","-| elf_class (`kind: integer`, D8 `d08_analysis_elf_class`) | the bit width `64` / `32` (single, TT, Mastery x5) | `2` / `1` (raw EI_CLASS byte; GM-rejected D8) |","-| machine (`kind: integer`, D8-D9 `d08`/`d09_analysis_machine`) | decimal e_machine (`62` = x86-64; read u16 at offset 18 in EI_DATA order) | — |","+| elf_class (`kind` exact_text) | `ELF64` / `ELF32` (readelf style) | ELFCLASS64 |","+| elf_class (`kind: integer`, D8) | the bit width `64` / `32` | `2` / `1` (raw EI_CLASS byte) |","+| machine (`kind: integer`, D8-D9) | decimal e_machine (`62` = x86-64; u16 at offset 18 in EI_DATA order) | — |"," | endianness | `little` / `big` | little endian, lsb, msb |"," | machine (ELF) | `x86-64`, `x86`, `AArch64`, `ARM` | EM_X86_64, x86_64, amd64 |"," | machine (PE FILE_HEADER) | 0x14c → `i386`; 0x8664 → `x86-64` | x86 (for PE i386); raw `0x8664` |","-| architecture | the same machine words (Go ELF amd64 → `x86-64`; Go PE `.exe` 0x8664 → `x86-64`) | amd64, arm64, 386, x86_64 |","+| architecture | the same machine words (Go ELF amd64 → `x86-64`; Go PE 0x8664 → `x86-64`) | amd64, arm64, 386, x86_64 |"," | elf_type | the constant `ET_EXEC` / `ET_DYN` | EXEC |"," | entry_point, crc32_hex, xor_key_hex | lowercase hex with `0x` (crc `0x%08x`, key `0x%02x`) | — |","-| recover_code | base-10 integer (`mov eax, 0x1fa4` → 8100); `none` if the named function is absent and the format allows it (inferred) | the renamed function's constant |","+| recover_code | base-10 integer (`mov eax, 0x1fa4` → 8100); `none` if the named function is absent and the format allows it | the renamed function's constant |"," | has_symtab / has_cpp_* | enum `true`/`false` | — |"," | marker | exact `.huntress` string without the NUL; `none` if the section is missing | — |"," | format (native) | lowercase container: `elf`, `pe` (`macho` presumed) | ELF, ELF64, elf64-x86-64, HCFG, json, exe, pe32+, coff, mz |","-| format (.NET) | `pe_cli` | ~50 synonyms (pe, pe32, dotnet, .net, cil, msil, clr, managed, assembly, ...) — lib/knowledge.py DOTNET_FORMAT_REJECTED |","+| format (.NET) | `pe_cli` | ~50 synonyms — lib/knowledge.py DOTNET_FORMAT_REJECTED |"," | format (Java/Kotlin jar) | `jar` (D6 Java, D7 Kotlin) | jar_jvm |","-| format / architecture (Swift D8, Nim D9, Zig D10, D D11, FPC D12, Crystal D13 ELF) | `elf` / `x86-64`; D9 machine integer `62` (source language never changes the container label) | — |","+| format / architecture (Swift, Nim, Zig, D, FPC, Crystal, ObjC ELF; D8-D14) | `elf` / `x86-64` (source language never changes the container label) | — |"," | C++ symbols (ELF) | bare Itanium mangled name (`_ZNK...`, `_ZTV...`) | the demangled form |"," | C++ symbols (PE/MinGW) | COMDAT section name `.text$<mangled>` (function), `.rdata$<mangled>` (vtable) | bare mangled name |"," | section_names (JSON) | pyelftools order INCLUDING the leading `\"\"` | list without \"\" |"," | symbols (JSON) | non-empty .symtab names, table order, dupes kept | list with the \"\" entries |","-| disassembly (JSON) | capstone intel `\"mov eax, 8100\"`, `\"ret\"`, decimal immediates (D6 text says AT&T is also accepted) | hex imm, `\"ret \"`, `mov eax,0x..` |","+| disassembly (JSON) | capstone intel `\"mov eax, 8100\"`, `\"ret\"`, decimal immediates | hex imm, `\"ret \"`, `mov eax,0x..` |"," | metadata_version | BSJB root string `v4.0.30319` | net8.0 / TFM / assembly version |"," | config_* | values verbatim from the decoded HCFG JSON (mutex keeps ONE backslash) | JSON-escaped `\\\\` |"," | hcfg_version | header byte 4 as a decimal integer | — |","-| has_hcfg_section (D10, enum) | `true` when a section is literally named `.hcfg` (ELF Zig + PE Zig both `true`) | — |","-| hcfg_offset (`kind: integer`, D9, D11-D13) | decimal FILE offset of the stored blob's first byte: base64 text start (Nim `30696`, D `368272`, Crystal `560188`), RAW blob = the `HCFG` magic (FPC `82928`), all modes | — (not tried: VA 0x4077e8, struct 0x77e0, `strings -t d` 30695) |","-| xor_key_hex | HCFG header byte 5 as `0x%02x` (D8: 0x51/0x61/0x71/0x31 for d04-d07) | — |","+| has_hcfg_section (D10, D14, enum) | `true` when a section is literally named `.hcfg` (Zig ELF/PE, ObjC ELF) | — |","+| hcfg_offset (`kind: integer`, D9, D11-D13) | decimal FILE offset of the stored blob's first byte: base64 text start (`30696`, `368272`, `560188`), RAW = the `HCFG` magic (`82928`) | — (not tried: VA, struct start, `strings -t d` offset-1) |","+| xor_key_hex | HCFG header byte 5 as `0x%02x` | — |"," | compression_methods (jar, `kind: json`) | sorted distinct ZIP `compress_type` ids, compact: `[0,8]` | — |"," Naming law (from playbook.py): native format = container only; a managed .NET binary = container_runtime from the spec tokens (pe+cli)."," Java broke the compound law (`jar`), so when a label is new, try the plain container name AND the compound, one per POST."," "," ## Pitfalls that cost time","-- **A multi-field POST is all-or-nothing.** One wrong field fails the set and hides which field was wrong. On D2 this made the correct `pe`","-  look rejected for hours (the real error was the symbol form). Submit unconfirmed/new fields ALONE; batch only the known ones.","+- **A multi-field POST is all-or-nothing.** One wrong field fails the set and hides which field was wrong (D2: correct `pe` looked","+  rejected for hours). Submit unconfirmed/new fields ALONE; batch only the known ones."," - **Guessing synonyms for a synthetic label** (D3 .NET format: ~50 tries, ~1.5 h). Derive from spec tokens and the playbook naming laws,","-  use `hctf labels` (it ranks candidates from the playbook), and read the question `syntax` first: the GM has started embedding hints.","+  use `hctf labels`, and read the question `syntax` first: the GM embeds hints.","+- **Chasing the prompt's theme** (D5-D14): the language flavour (selectors, protocols, coroutines, record layouts) has never been","+  asked since D4. Read the contract ids first; reverse only what an id asks for."," - **Shell/JSON quoting** of `Global\\Huntress...` mutexes: build the submit JSON with python/jq, not by hand in a shell string."," - **capstone `ret` has an empty op_str**: `f\"{m} {o}\"` gives `\"ret \"`. Strip it, and convert immediates to decimal.","-- **Cumulative zip**: check whether the old groups' sha256 match a previous day's confirmed bytes. If yes, those answers carry over;","-  spend the time on the NEW group only (D4-D6 took minutes because of this).","+- **Cumulative zip**: old groups' answers carry over when their sha256 match; spend the time on the NEW group only."," - **Recursive unzip** destroys nested containers (.jar/.apk) and their `dNN--` prefix; keep them whole.","-- **Same field name, different `kind`** (D8 elf_class/machine): a solver keyed only on the field name emits `ELF64` for an integer","-  question. Read `answer_format.kind` per id.","-- **Huge members** (D8: 67 MB Swift static-stdlib ELF): any per-key xor brute force or per-field re-parse blows a 10 s window.","-  Cheap encodings first (raw magic, base64 magic `SENGR`), crc-gate every hit, parse each member once.","-- **Decoy magics** (D9 Nim): the code that CHECKS the magic embeds `\"HCFG\"` (and an assert message) as literals, so the first","-  raw hit is not the blob. A decoder that returns on the first crc-\"valid\" hit (empty len 0 => crc32(b\"\")==0 passes!) stops","-  early; require non-empty JSON that parses, then keep scanning, then try the base64 form.","-- **Location fields per scan path** (D12): a decoder with raw AND base64 branches must return the hit offset from BOTH;","-  the raw branch's missing offset cost 2 POSTs. Before submitting, assert no `none` where a config was decoded.","-- **`strings -t d` offsets on Nim/Swift literals**: the byte before the text can be printable (Nim's strlit flag 0x40 = `@`), so","-  `strings` reports offset-1 (30695). Take offsets from `grep -abo`/`re.finditer(...).start()` on the exact token.","+- **Same field name, different `kind`** (D8 elf_class/machine): read `answer_format.kind` per id.","+- **Huge members** (D8: 67 MB Swift): any per-key xor brute force or per-field re-parse blows a timed window. Cheap encodings first","+  (raw magic, base64 `SENGR`), crc-gate every hit, parse each member once.","+- **Decoy magics** (D9 Nim): code that CHECKS the magic embeds `\"HCFG\"` literals. Empty len 0 => crc32(b\"\")==0 passes! Require","+  non-empty JSON that parses, keep scanning, then try the base64 form.","+- **Location fields per scan path** (D12): a decoder with raw AND base64 branches must return the hit offset from BOTH. Before","+  submitting, assert no `none` where a config was decoded.","+- **`strings -t d` offsets on Nim/Swift literals**: a printable byte before the text shifts the offset by 1. Use `grep -abo` /","+  `re.finditer(...).start()` on the exact token."," - **Jar members are deflated**: `grep HCFG file.jar` finds nothing. Inflate the class, read constant-pool strings, base64-decode.","-  In a fat jar (Kotlin/Scala/shaded) scan the Main-Class first; a full scan of ~3000 runtime classes eats timed windows.","-- **Stripped builds** in variants (D1 slot, D2 Mastery set2, D8 Mastery d01): no recover_code symbol. Answer what the question","-  defines for absence (`[]` for the disassembly, `none` where allowed), has_symtab=false. The old leaf `mov eax, imm; ret` guess","-  failed all 5 D8 Mastery sets.","-- **Renamed designated function** (D1 TT section-beacon): the question still says recover_code. Answer `none` (when the format allows it), not the other function's constant.","-- **Tool parity** (2026-10-07): ilspycmd, dotnet, rustfilt, GoReSym (`GoReSym -t -p file`), rabin2 are installed in","-  `bin/`; monodis/de4dot are not (dnfile covers .NET metadata).","-- **Timed windows are ~6-12 s** (TT; D9 TT 10 s, Mastery 20-27 s for 5 sets, download is ~half of it): D2 TT/Mastery attempts expired from download/orchestration latency, not solver speed (the solver ran in 0.3-0.5 s).","-  After editing hctf/*.py, restart the orchestrator. D1/D2 runs used stale modules and kept sending only the slot0 ids.","+- **Stripped builds / renamed functions** in variants (D1 TT, D2 Mastery set2, D8 Mastery d01): answer what the question defines","+  for absence (`[]`, `none`, has_symtab=false); never substitute a heuristic constant.","+- **Speed flags measured under load** (D12, D14): \"N s on single_solve\" from a parallel solver-test is contention; re-measure","+  pinned and isolated before touching code.","+- **Tool parity**: ilspycmd, dotnet, rustfilt, GoReSym, rabin2, swift-demangle are in `bin/`; monodis/de4dot are not.","+- **Timed windows** (6-30 s; download is a big share of a 3-5 set Mastery): early TT/Mastery expiries were download/orchestration","+  latency, not solver speed. After editing hctf/*.py, restart the orchestrator (D1/D2 ran stale modules)."," - **PE machine map must include 0x8664 → `x86-64`**: a from-scratch replay once emitted `0x8664` and failed TT twice."]}],"originalFile":"# binary-reverse-engineering — technique log (days 1-13; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (OBSERVATIONS, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- One `evidence.zip` (AES, password `infected`). From Day 3 on it is CUMULATIVE: members `dNN--variant-XXX.<ext>`, one group per\n  past day, plus ONE new container/language per day: D1 C ELF, D2 C++ (ELF or MinGW PE32+), D3 .NET dll (+runtimeconfig.json),\n  D4 static stripped Go ELF, D5 static Rust ELF (debug_info), D6 Java .jar, D7 Kotlin fat .jar (5 MB, ~3300 entries), D8 Swift ELF\n  (67 MB, static stdlib+Foundation+ICU, not stripped), D9 Nim ELF (60 KB, dynamic glibc, not stripped), D10 Zig ELF (134 KB,\n  dynamic glibc, stripped, clang/LLD 19 zig-bootstrap in `.comment`) -- a Zig PE `.exe` in Mastery set2, D11 D-language ELF (1 MB,\n  DMD, druntime static + dynamic glibc, not stripped, debug_info), D12 Free Pascal ELF (100 KB, FPC 3.2.2, static, stripped), D13 Crystal ELF (749 KB, dynamic glibc + libgc, not\n  stripped).\n  Answer ids `dNN_artifact_sha256_K` / `dNN_analysis_<field>`.\n- From Day 2 on, every new-day member carries the same embedded **HCFG** config blob: `'HCFG' | u8 ver | u8 xor_key | u16 len (LE) |\n  u32 crc32 | xor'd JSON` (JSON at offset 12; crc32 is over the decoded plaintext). Only its storage location changes\n  (`.hcfg` section, .NET FieldRVA array, Go/Rust rodata, base64'd in a Java/Kotlin constant pool, base64 Swift String literal in\n  `.rodata` on D8, base64 Nim/D string literal in `.rodata` on D9/D11, RAW in FPC `.data` on D12, base64 Crystal String literal in `.rodata` on D13). Scan raw bytes for `HCFG` AND for its base64 form `SENGR...` (raw `HCFG` can also be a false hit inside code: check crc).\n  The JSON also carries never-asked keys (ipv4, windows_path, linux_path, service, host_model on D7): parse the whole dict so a new `config_<key>` id is free.\n- The analysis is easy (headers, symbols, one config blob). The hard part is the GM's exact label for a few `exact_text` fields (format,\n  machine, disassembly, symbol). The question set grows each day (9 → 17 → 24 → 32 → 40 → 48 → 56 → 80 → 90 → 100 → 110 → 120 → 130 fields); old groups reuse the same bytes,\n  but D8 BACKFILLED old groups to 10 ids each (new: has_symtab, has_cpp_typeinfo/vtable, xor_key_hex, hcfg_version, compression_methods).\n- The prompt's theme (Rust panics, D7 \"coroutine state machine\", D8 Swift \"protocols\", D9 Nim \"runtime fingerprints\") has NOT\n  been asked since D4: the new group gets sha256, format, config_campaign/domain/mutex/url/crc32_hex + 1-3 extra ids\n  (architecture D4-D5/D8-D12, hcfg_version D6-D7, elf_class/machine as INTEGERS D8-D9, `hcfg_offset` D9 + D11 + D12, `has_hcfg_section`\n  D10). D11/D12/D13 added NO new field (D12 = hcfg_offset on a RAW blob; D13 \"follow the DNS labels\" = just the\n  config domain/url). Usually exactly ONE\n  never-seen field per day: grep the new group's ids against the solver's field table before anything else.\n- Time Trial ≈ 6-16 s; Mastery = `setN.` prefixed copies, 2 sets (7-12 s) through D7, 5 sets / 400-450 ids / 20-27 s on D8-D9,\n  3 sets / 300-390 ids / 28-30 s on D10-D12 (TT 30 s too; D13 TT 80 s / Mastery 200 s); artifacts are named `delivery N: evidence.zip`.\n- **D10 RELAXED the label fields**: 36 ids are now `kind: pattern` whose syntax ACCEPTS equivalents (format: \"ELF or PE; case,\n  ELF32/ELF64/PE32/PE32+ accepted\"; machine/architecture: \"standard tool or symbolic label, or decimal/hex code\"; e_type and\n  endianness: symbolic constant / readelf label / numeric code; .NET format: any container_runtime token with CLI/CLR/.NET). D8-D9's\n  integer machine became pattern. Keep emitting the GM-confirmed spellings; the old REJECTED lists may be stale for pattern ids.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **HCFG location / encoding** -- same blob, different storage per container (`.hcfg` section, .NET FieldRVA, Go/Rust rodata,\n  base64 inside a Java/Kotlin constant pool, base64 Swift/Nim string literal in ELF `.rodata` on D8/D9): scan raw bytes for `HCFG`\n  and for `SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]*=*` (base64 of `HCFG`, std or urlsafe), decode, accept only if crc32(plain) matches AND the JSON\n  parses -- keep scanning past a failing hit (D9 Nim had two raw `HCFG` decoys); never a fixed offset.\n- **Location-as-answer (`hcfg_offset`, D9/D11/D12)** -- base-10 FILE offset of the first byte of the stored blob as it sits in\n  the member: base64 form -> the `S` of `SENGR...` (D9 Nim 30696, D11 D 368272, D13 Crystal 560188 -- the text, not the String header 12 B before it); RAW form -> the `H` of `HCFG` (D12 FPC 82928 =\n  0x143f0 in `.data`, GM-confirmed single+TT+Mastery x3). Constant across a day's variants although shas differ -- still\n  compute it: record `m.start()` of whichever scan hit (raw OR base64) validated, on BOTH paths (D12's raw path returned `none`).\n- **Any other storage encoding -> `lib.binary.hcfg_scan(data, deadline=None)`** (Day 14 prep; pure stdlib, Homebase-safe,\n  ~15 ms / 2 MB, ~30 ms / 4 MB real ELF, ~0.6 s / 67 MB). Returns every `HcfgHit` (offset, encoding, version, key, length, crc,\n  crc_ok, config, plain, speculative, detail) best first; take `lib.binary.hcfg_find(data)` (first crc-valid + JSON-parsing hit).\n  Covers raw, base64 (std / url / newline-wrapped), hex (plain, `48 43`, `48:43`, `\\x48`, `0x48, `), base32 (upper/lower),\n  base85, ascii85 (`<~` optional), UTF-16LE/BE of raw/base64/hex/base32/base85, reversed raw, reversed base64, single-byte\n  xor'd base64 / xor'd raw (key-independent xor-diff search), zlib, gzip, raw deflate (fixed-Huffman anchor anywhere; headerless\n  dynamic brute force only while nothing valid was found and the file is <= 1 MiB, `HCTF_HCFG_DEFLATE_MAX`). Decoys (bad crc,\n  truncated, bare `\"HCFG\"` strings, wrong magic) come back with `valid=False`. Offset convention per encoding (`hcfg_offset`):\n\n  | encoding | offset = | status |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | raw | the `H` of the magic | GM-confirmed (D12) |\n  | base64 | first base64 char (`S` of `SENGR`) | GM-confirmed (D9/D11/D13) |\n  | base64url, base32, base85, hex, hex-sep | first char of the stored text (`\\` of `\\x48`, `0` of `0x48`) | speculative |\n  | ascii85 | the `<` of `<~` if present, else first char | speculative |\n  | utf16le-* / utf16be-* | first byte of the first code unit (BE: its `00`); LE/BE tie -> the 2-aligned reading, else LE | speculative |\n  | reversed-raw / reversed-base64 | lowest file offset of the reversed region (where the blob's LAST byte / the `=` pad sits) | speculative |\n  | xor-base64 / xor-raw | first stored byte (`detail` = `xor=0x..`) | speculative |\n  | zlib / gzip / deflate | first byte of the compressed stream (`78`, `1f 8b`, the deflate block header) | speculative |\n\n  Wired into the newest binary solver (D13 `native_hcfg` + `jar_hcfg`): runs only when the D13 scan finds nothing, or when its\n  hit parses but fails crc32 (then a crc-valid blob elsewhere wins). Kill switch `HCTF_HCFG_SCAN_EXT=0` = the D13 behaviour\n  exactly. A speculative offset is a first guess: if the GM rejects it, try the offset of the container header in front of\n  the stored form (String header, length prefix, `<~` / quote) next. Fixtures: `tests/data/hcfg_fixtures/` (`make.py`); checks in\n  `tests/test_day14_s4.py`.\n- **xor key / config values** -- re-roll per variant; derive from the header byte, never from the sample.\n- **Container per member** -- ELF vs PE32+ `.exe` re-rolls per member: Mastery set2 had d02 C++ as `.exe` (D3-D5, D7, D10) and d04\n  Go as `.exe` (D4, D5, D7, D10); D6 set2 had both as ELF; D10 set2 had the NEW d10 Zig member as a PE too (format `pe`). Labels come from the header of THIS member (Go PE: format `pe`, architecture `x86-64` from Machine).\n- **Variant index per group** -- `dNN--variant-XXX` re-rolls per group and mode (D7 TT: d03-001, d04-006, d07-005 ...); sizes\n  and config values change, names/layout don't. TT == Mastery set1 bytes on D7; D8 TT re-used the D7 TT old-group indices\n  (d08 = variant-000); D9 TT == set1 for d02-d09 (d09 BR09-003) but d01 differed (TT variant-000 `8100`, all 5 Mastery sets one\n  other d01 with `mov eax, 8104`, symtab present). Mastery d09 = BR09-003/006/001/004/007; d08 stayed variant-000..004.\n- **Mastery packaging** -- `setN.` prefixed ids, each set its own `delivery N: evidence.zip` (same filename): pair by sha256.\n  Set count re-rolls: 2 (D2-D7), 5 on D8-D9 (set2/set4 had d02/d04 as PE both days), 3 on D10: loop over every `setN.`. From D9 (all\n  lanes) the first question of each set ends `Evidence case: d09-m-<16hex>. [assigned-artifact-sha256:<zip sha256>]`\n  (TT: `d09-tt-...`): an explicit set -> delivery map; it is question TEXT, never part of an answer.\n- **answer_format.kind for the same field name** -- D8: `d01_analysis_elf_class`/`machine` exact_text (`ELF64`/`x86-64`) and\n  `d08_analysis_elf_class`/`machine` integer (`64`/`62`) in ONE contract; D9 `d09_analysis_machine` integer again. Rule:\n  dispatch on `kind`, not on the field name.\n- **Feature-presence fields** -- `has_<thing>_section` (D10 `has_hcfg_section`, enum true/false) for ELF AND PE: answer from the\n  member's section-name table (`.hcfg` literally; PE names are 8-byte NUL-padded), generic over `<thing>` (regex `has_(\\w+?)_section`).\n- **Field set per old group** -- old groups gain ids over days (D8 padded every group to 10). Answer by field name from the\n  parsed facts dict of THAT member; an unknown field must log and fall through, never crash. Keep the older 56/112-id cases passing.\n  D9 kept D8's 10 ids for d01-d08 (d08: sha, architecture, elf_class, format, machine, 5 config) and added d09 with `hcfg_offset`.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `evidence.zip`, \"AES Encrypted\" | `7z x -pinfected -y evidence.zip` (Python: `pyzipper`); `sha256sum *` for every `artifact_sha256_K` (K = archive order within the group) |\n| `readelf -h -S` hint, ELF header questions | `readelf -hSW`, `readelf -sW`; `readelf -x .huntress` / `readelf -p .huntress` for the custom-section marker |\n| \"constant returned by recover_code\" / `disassembly` | `objdump -d -M intel --no-show-raw-insn` around `<recover_code>`; capstone on the FUNC symbol's st_value..st_size bytes |\n| Stripped C build, no `.symtab` | find the leaf `b8 imm32 c3` (`mov eax, imm; ret`) in `.text` (`lib.binary.recover_return_constants`) and check it against what `main` inlines |\n| C++ / \"mangled\" / \"vtable\" / \"RTTI\" | `nm -C` / `c++filt`; look for `_ZTV<class>` (vtable), `_ZTI`/`_ZTS` (typeinfo), `_ZNK<cls>5scoreEPKc`; the PE COFF symtab: `objdump -t file.exe` |\n| `PE32+` MinGW `.exe` | `objdump -t` (COFF symbols + string table), `pefile` (Machine, OPTIONAL_HEADER.Magic, sections incl. `.hcfg`) |\n| \"CLI metadata\", `.dll` + `runtimeconfig.json`, `BSJB` in strings | `ilspycmd file.dll` (decompile to C#; installed 2026-10-07) or Python `dnfile`; config = `<PrivateImplementationDetails>` FieldRVA static array; `strings` shows `BSJB v4.0.30319` |\n| Go (\"build info, function names, file paths\") | `go version -m file` (buildinfo: go1.x, GOARCH); `lib.binary.go_buildinfo` / `go_pclntab_funcs` (stripped names survive in `.gopclntab`) |\n| Rust (\"mangled symbols with a distinct accent\", panic strings) | `readelf -hS` + `HCFG` scan was enough on D5; demangle with `rustfilt` (installed) or `lib.binary.rustfilt` (binary) if symbols are asked |\n| `.jar` / \"constant pool\" | unzip the jar, read `META-INF/MANIFEST.MF` Main-Class, `javap -v -p Main.class`; look for `ConstantValue: String` (`static final String CONFIG`) |\n| Kotlin fat jar (`kotlin/` runtime, `META-INF/main.kotlin_module`, `X$fn$1 extends ContinuationImpl` with `int label`) | Same as `.jar`: parse the Main-Class first, skip `kotlin/`/`org/jetbrains/`. Coroutine \"state machine\" = `invokeSuspend` switching on `label`; branch logic is plain `javap -c` (`lookupswitch` on String.hashCode + `ldc` results) |\n| Swift ELF (`swift5_*` sections, `$s<len><Module>...` symbols, clang `swiftlang` in `.comment`, huge 60+ MB static stdlib) | `nm FILE \\| grep '\\$s[0-9]*<Module>'` (app symbols sit just after `frame_dummy`); `bin/swift-demangle`; config getter = `lea rax,[rip+X]; movabs rax,0xd0000000000001fc; ret` → literal chars at X+0x20, count = low 48 bits (0x1fc); or simply regex `SENGR` base64 |\n| Nim ELF (`NimMain`/`NimMainModule`/`PreMain`, `TM__<hash>_N` literals, `<proc>__<mod>_u<N>` mangling e.g. `encodedConfig__v000_u31`, `@m..@snim@slib@s...nim.c` / `fatal.nim` strings, `nimZeroMem`/`nimCopyMem`) | It is plain C-compiled ELF: header ids via readelf as usual. Config proc returns a string literal: `mov eax,0x1fc; lea rdx,[rip+X]` (len, `TM__` ptr); the literal is `u64 cap\\|0x4000000000000000` then the chars, so text = X+8 (file off = VA - segment base). Or regex `SENGR` |\n| D ELF (`_D<len><module>...` mangling e.g. `_D4v00012decodeConfigFZAya`, `_D2rt`/`_D4core` druntime symbols, `DMDH`/`DMDI` strings, no `.comment`) | Plain native ELF: readelf header ids as usual. Config = `decodeConfig()` returning a D string (`Aya` = immutable(char)[]); the base64 `SENGR...` literal is NUL-terminated in `.rodata` -- regex it. `evaluate`/`campaign` funcs exist but were never asked |\n| Free Pascal ELF (`FPC 3.2.2 [...] for x86_64 - Linux` string, `.fpcdata` section, static + stripped, `FPC_`/`fpc_` RTL names in strings) | Plain native ELF: readelf header ids as usual. HCFG sits RAW (magic + header + XOR'd JSON) in `.data` -- `grep -abo HCFG`, crc-gate, offset = the magic's offset. Pascal \"record layouts\" flavour unasked |\n| Crystal ELF (`Crystal:H` strings, Boehm GC exports `GC_malloc`/`GC_world_stopped`, `*crystal*` symbols via `nm`) | Plain native ELF: readelf header ids as usual. Config = base64 `SENGR...` Crystal String literal in `.rodata` behind a 12-byte header (`u32 type_id=1, u32 bytesize, u32 length`) -- regex it; offset = the `S`. \"DNS labels\" = the config's domain/url, no DNS wire format anywhere |\n| Packed / high entropy / `UPX!` | `lib.binary.packer_info` → `upx -d` on a COPY (not seen yet) |\n| Real code-reversing question (not seen yet) | `rizin -q -c \"aaa; pdf @ sym.<fn>\"`; Ghidra headless `lib.binary.ghidra_decompile` (heavy, last resort) |\n\n## Day by day\n**D1 \"ELF Aware\"** (9 Qs; ~14 min, 4 wrong). C ELF64: class, endianness, machine, e_type, `.huntress` marker, has_symtab,\nrecover_code constant, entry point (readelf/objdump; pyelftools + capstone). Spellings learned by rejection. TT \"slot\" bundle\n(`slotN_<qid>`): stripped profile and a renamed designated fn (→ `none`, unconfirmed).\n\n**D2 \"Mangled\"** (17 Qs; ~22 min, 5 wrong). + C++ (ELF or MinGW PE32+). First HCFG (`.hcfg` section). vtable = `_ZTV<class owning\nscore>`; PE symbol fields want COMDAT `.text$<mangled>` / `.rdata$<mangled>` (all-or-nothing set POSTs hid this for hours).\n\n**D3 \"Table Manners\"** (24 Qs; ~1 h 48 min, ~60 wrong). + .NET 8 PE32 i386 dll: `dnfile` → BSJB `v4.0.30319`, FieldRVA HCFG.\n`d03_analysis_format` = `pe_cli` after ~50 rejected synonyms: compose labels from spec tokens.\n\n**D4 \"Go Fish\"** (32 Qs; ~1.5 min, 1 wrong). Static stripped Go ELF; HCFG in rodata. `architecture` `amd64` (GOARCH) REJECTED →\n`x86-64`: \"architecture\" uses the container's machine words, not the toolchain token.\n\n**D5 \"Rust Belt\"** (40 Qs; 7 s, 0 wrong, no LLM). Static Rust ELF; the D4 solver passed unchanged. Rust theme never asked.\n\n**D6 \"Pool Party\"** (48 Qs; ~5 min, 1 wrong). `.jar`: Main-Class `javap -v -p` → `static final String CONFIG` base64 → HCFG. New\n`hcfg_version` (byte 4, base-10). Format `jar_jvm` REJECTED → `jar`. Keep nested .jar/.apk members whole (recursive unzip lost the\n`d06--` prefix). Question texts got rewritten to name accepted spellings: read each `syntax`.\n\n**D7 \"Routine Check\"** (56 Qs; 3 min, 0 wrong). 5 MB Kotlin fat jar, same constant-pool base64 HCFG; scan the Main-Class first\n(not ~3300 runtime classes). Unasked \"state machine\": `evaluate()` lookupswitch on env `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`.\n\n**D8 \"Swift Justice\"** (80 Qs). New d08 = 67 MB static Swift ELF (~290k symbols, not stripped); old groups backfilled to 10 ids.\n- **Read `answer_format.kind` first:** d08 elf_class/machine were `integer` → bit width `64` (not EI_CLASS `2`) and `62`.\n- Eager `pyelftools` `iter_symbols()` and the headerless-XOR brute force each took 60 s+ on it (worker lost 120 s + a 66 s\n  profile). Recon with `readelf`/`nm`/`strings`; config = base64 HCFG in `.rodata` (`strings -n 40 | grep -m3 '^SENGR'`).\n- Mastery: 5 deliveries x ~31 MB; download ~4.6-10 s + solve ~8 s inside a 27 s window.\n- **Mastery mutated a carry-over ELF:** a STRIPPED d01 (no .symtab). The question says \"If that symbol is absent, submit []\";\n  the old \"last `mov eax, imm32; ret` leaf\" fallback answered `[\"mov eax, 8102\",\"ret\"]` and failed all 5 sets. Absent →\n  `[]`, has_symtab `false`, symbols `[]`. Never substitute a heuristic for an absence the question defines.\n- LIB: `lib.elf.fields(data)[1]` returns `elf_class_int`/`machine_int` for `kind == \"integer\"`.\n\n**D9 \"Nimble\"** (90 Qs; 86 s, 0 wrong). 60 KB Nim ELF (`.symtab` kept). Two raw `HCFG` DECOYS (assert text + magic-check\nliteral) -> the real blob is base64 `SENGR...` in a Nim literal (8-byte cap header before the text). NEW `hcfg_offset` = 30696 =\nfirst base64 char. Lost: a jq `.answer_id` (contract questions use `.id`). TT 10 s / Mastery 5 sets 20 s, both first try.\n\n**D10 \"Zig Zag\"** (100 Qs; ~33 s, 0 wrong). 134 KB stripped Zig ELF; HCFG raw in a writable `.hcfg` section. NEW enum\n`has_hcfg_section` = `true` (generic `has_(\\w+?)_section` over section names, ELF and PE). \"ELF and PE side by side\" only meant\nMastery set2's d10 was a Zig PE (format `pe`). TT in_window 2.85 s, Mastery 3 sets 5.59 s.\n\n**D11 \"D-Day\"** (110 Qs; ~36 s, 0 wrong). 1 MB DMD ELF; base64 HCFG NUL-terminated in `.rodata` after `.debug_line\\0`,\nhcfg_offset 368272. Carried-over solver answered everything (2 tool calls); \"template expansions\" flavour unasked.\n\n**D12 \"Pascal's Wager\"** (120 Qs; ~54 s start->CORRECT, 2 wrong POSTs). Prompt: \"Pascal is betting you won't read its record\nlayouts ... read the configuration straight from memory's own filing cabinet.\" New d12 = `d12--variant-000.elf`, 100,976 B Free\nPascal 3.2.2 ELF64 x86-64, static, stripped. d12 ids: sha, architecture, format, machine, 5 config, hcfg_offset (no new field).\n- HCFG RAW in `.data` at file offset 0x143f0 (`HCFG 01 81 7001 f881fce4` = ver 1, key 0x81, len 368) -> `hcfg_offset` **82928**\n  (offset of the magic itself); config `BR12-000` / `node-000.day12.example.invalid` / crc `0xe4fc81f8`.\n- The copied D11 solver decoded the raw blob but its raw-scan branch did not record the offset -> `none`. POST 1 (120 ids)\n  incorrect; the harness bisect POSTed d01-d06 (accepted) then d07-d12 (incorrect); worker `xxd -s 82900`, patched the raw\n  branch to return its offset (+ keep scanning past a raw decoy whose crc fails), CORRECT. Lesson: every scan path must\n  fill every location field.\n- TT 30 s window, in_window 2.9 s (BR12-004); Mastery 3 sets / 360 ids, in_window 5.14 s (BR12-004/005/006, offset 82928 in\n  all). Both CORRECT first try.\n\n**D13 \"Crystal Clear\"** (130 Qs; ~14 s start->CORRECT, 0 wrong, no worker tool call). Prompt: \"Crystal compiles to native code\nwith a distinctive shine. Fingerprint the runtime, then follow the DNS labels\". New d13 = `d13--variant-000.elf`, 749,208 B\nCrystal ELF64 x86-64 (dynamic, libgc, symtab). d13 ids: sha, architecture, machine, format, 5 config, hcfg_offset (no new field).\n- Base64 HCFG in a Crystal String literal (`01000000 fc010000 fc010000` header, 508 chars) -> `hcfg_offset` **560188** (0x88c3c,\n  first base64 char); `BR13-000` / `node-000.day13.example.invalid` / crc `0xa69b7e61`, key 0x91. Domain never in plaintext.\n- The carried-over solver's `SENGR` regex + `m.start()` answered every field. TT (80 s window) in_window 2.41 s; Mastery 3 sets /\n  390 ids in_window 5.99 s (variants 007/002/005; key = 0x91+N; offset constant). Both CORRECT first try.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n| Field family | Accepted form | Rejected (never resubmit) |\n|---|---|---|\n| elf_class (`answer_format.kind` exact_text) | `ELF64` / `ELF32` (readelf style) | ELFCLASS64 |\n| elf_class (`kind: integer`, D8 `d08_analysis_elf_class`) | the bit width `64` / `32` (single, TT, Mastery x5) | `2` / `1` (raw EI_CLASS byte; GM-rejected D8) |\n| machine (`kind: integer`, D8-D9 `d08`/`d09_analysis_machine`) | decimal e_machine (`62` = x86-64; read u16 at offset 18 in EI_DATA order) | — |\n| endianness | `little` / `big` | little endian, lsb, msb |\n| machine (ELF) | `x86-64`, `x86`, `AArch64`, `ARM` | EM_X86_64, x86_64, amd64 |\n| machine (PE FILE_HEADER) | 0x14c → `i386`; 0x8664 → `x86-64` | x86 (for PE i386); raw `0x8664` |\n| architecture | the same machine words (Go ELF amd64 → `x86-64`; Go PE `.exe` 0x8664 → `x86-64`) | amd64, arm64, 386, x86_64 |\n| elf_type | the constant `ET_EXEC` / `ET_DYN` | EXEC |\n| entry_point, crc32_hex, xor_key_hex | lowercase hex with `0x` (crc `0x%08x`, key `0x%02x`) | — |\n| recover_code | base-10 integer (`mov eax, 0x1fa4` → 8100); `none` if the named function is absent and the format allows it (inferred) | the renamed function's constant |\n| has_symtab / has_cpp_* | enum `true`/`false` | — |\n| marker | exact `.huntress` string without the NUL; `none` if the section is missing | — |\n| format (native) | lowercase container: `elf`, `pe` (`macho` presumed) | ELF, ELF64, elf64-x86-64, HCFG, json, exe, pe32+, coff, mz |\n| format (.NET) | `pe_cli` | ~50 synonyms (pe, pe32, dotnet, .net, cil, msil, clr, managed, assembly, ...) — lib/knowledge.py DOTNET_FORMAT_REJECTED |\n| format (Java/Kotlin jar) | `jar` (D6 Java, D7 Kotlin) | jar_jvm |\n| format / architecture (Swift D8, Nim D9, Zig D10, D D11, FPC D12, Crystal D13 ELF) | `elf` / `x86-64`; D9 machine integer `62` (source language never changes the container label) | — |\n| C++ symbols (ELF) | bare Itanium mangled name (`_ZNK...`, `_ZTV...`) | the demangled form |\n| C++ symbols (PE/MinGW) | COMDAT section name `.text$<mangled>` (function), `.rdata$<mangled>` (vtable) | bare mangled name |\n| section_names (JSON) | pyelftools order INCLUDING the leading `\"\"` | list without \"\" |\n| symbols (JSON) | non-empty .symtab names, table order, dupes kept | list with the \"\" entries |\n| disassembly (JSON) | capstone intel `\"mov eax, 8100\"`, `\"ret\"`, decimal immediates (D6 text says AT&T is also accepted) | hex imm, `\"ret \"`, `mov eax,0x..` |\n| metadata_version | BSJB root string `v4.0.30319` | net8.0 / TFM / assembly version |\n| config_* | values verbatim from the decoded HCFG JSON (mutex keeps ONE backslash) | JSON-escaped `\\\\` |\n| hcfg_version | header byte 4 as a decimal integer | — |\n| has_hcfg_section (D10, enum) | `true` when a section is literally named `.hcfg` (ELF Zig + PE Zig both `true`) | — |\n| hcfg_offset (`kind: integer`, D9, D11-D13) | decimal FILE offset of the stored blob's first byte: base64 text start (Nim `30696`, D `368272`, Crystal `560188`), RAW blob = the `HCFG` magic (FPC `82928`), all modes | — (not tried: VA 0x4077e8, struct 0x77e0, `strings -t d` 30695) |\n| xor_key_hex | HCFG header byte 5 as `0x%02x` (D8: 0x51/0x61/0x71/0x31 for d04-d07) | — |\n| compression_methods (jar, `kind: json`) | sorted distinct ZIP `compress_type` ids, compact: `[0,8]` | — |\nNaming law (from playbook.py): native format = container only; a managed .NET binary = container_runtime from the spec tokens (pe+cli).\nJava broke the compound law (`jar`), so when a label is new, try the plain container name AND the compound, one per POST.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **A multi-field POST is all-or-nothing.** One wrong field fails the set and hides which field was wrong. On D2 this made the correct `pe`\n  look rejected for hours (the real error was the symbol form). Submit unconfirmed/new fields ALONE; batch only the known ones.\n- **Guessing synonyms for a synthetic label** (D3 .NET format: ~50 tries, ~1.5 h). Derive from spec tokens and the playbook naming laws,\n  use `hctf labels` (it ranks candidates from the playbook), and read the question `syntax` first: the GM has started embedding hints.\n- **Shell/JSON quoting** of `Global\\Huntress...` mutexes: build the submit JSON with python/jq, not by hand in a shell string.\n- **capstone `ret` has an empty op_str**: `f\"{m} {o}\"` gives `\"ret \"`. Strip it, and convert immediates to decimal.\n- **Cumulative zip**: check whether the old groups' sha256 match a previous day's confirmed bytes. If yes, those answers carry over;\n  spend the time on the NEW group only (D4-D6 took minutes because of this).\n- **Recursive unzip** destroys nested containers (.jar/.apk) and their `dNN--` prefix; keep them whole.\n- **Same field name, different `kind`** (D8 elf_class/machine): a solver keyed only on the field name emits `ELF64` for an integer\n  question. Read `answer_format.kind` per id.\n- **Huge members** (D8: 67 MB Swift static-stdlib ELF): any per-key xor brute force or per-field re-parse blows a 10 s window.\n  Cheap encodings first (raw magic, base64 magic `SENGR`), crc-gate every hit, parse each member once.\n- **Decoy magics** (D9 Nim): the code that CHECKS the magic embeds `\"HCFG\"` (and an assert message) as literals, so the first\n  raw hit is not the blob. A decoder that returns on the first crc-\"valid\" hit (empty len 0 => crc32(b\"\")==0 passes!) stops\n  early; require non-empty JSON that parses, then keep scanning, then try the base64 form.\n- **Location fields per scan path** (D12): a decoder with raw AND base64 branches must return the hit offset from BOTH;\n  the raw branch's missing offset cost 2 POSTs. Before submitting, assert no `none` where a config was decoded.\n- **`strings -t d` offsets on Nim/Swift literals**: the byte before the text can be printable (Nim's strlit flag 0x40 = `@`), so\n  `strings` reports offset-1 (30695). Take offsets from `grep -abo`/`re.finditer(...).start()` on the exact token.\n- **Jar members are deflated**: `grep HCFG file.jar` finds nothing. Inflate the class, read constant-pool strings, base64-decode.\n  In a fat jar (Kotlin/Scala/shaded) scan the Main-Class first; a full scan of ~3000 runtime classes eats timed windows.\n- **Stripped builds** in variants (D1 slot, D2 Mastery set2, D8 Mastery d01): no recover_code symbol. Answer what the question\n  defines for absence (`[]` for the disassembly, `none` where allowed), has_symtab=false. The old leaf `mov eax, imm; ret` guess\n  failed all 5 D8 Mastery sets.\n- **Renamed designated function** (D1 TT section-beacon): the question still says recover_code. Answer `none` (when the format allows it), not the other function's constant.\n- **Tool parity** (2026-10-07): ilspycmd, dotnet, rustfilt, GoReSym (`GoReSym -t -p file`), rabin2 are installed in\n  `bin/`; monodis/de4dot are not (dnfile covers .NET metadata).\n- **Timed windows are ~6-12 s** (TT; D9 TT 10 s, Mastery 20-27 s for 5 sets, download is ~half of it): D2 TT/Mastery attempts expired from download/orchestration latency, not solver speed (the solver ran in 0.3-0.5 s).\n  After editing hctf/*.py, restart the orchestrator. D1/D2 runs used stale modules and kept sending only the slot0 ids.\n- **PE machine map must include 0x8664 → `x86-64`**: a from-scratch replay once emitted `0x8664` and failed TT twice.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Tzq2PB96yTe1TLQyvpVLLQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
